That they a city may prepare"}, {"text": "commodiously to live."}]}, {"index": 27, "lines": [{"text": "There sow they fields, and vineyards plant,", "syllables": ["There", "sow", "they", "fields,", "and", "vineya-", "rds", "plant,"], "bibleVerseRef": 37}, {"text": "to yield fruits of increase.", "syllables": ["to", "yield", "fruits", "of", "increa-", "se."]}, {"text": "His blessing makes them multiply,", "bibleVerseRef": 38}, {"text": "lets not their beasts decrease."}]}, {"index": 28, "lines": [{"text": "Again they are diminished,", "bibleVerseRef": 39}, {"text": "and very low brought down,"}, {"text": "Through sorrow and affliction,", "syllables": ["Throu-", "gh", "sor-", "row", "and", "af-", "flic-", "tion,"]}, {"text": "and great oppression.", "syllables": ["and", "grea-", "t", "op-", "pres-", "sion."]}]}, {"index": 29, "lines": [{"text": "He upon princes pours contempt,", "bibleVerseRef": 40}, {"text": "and causeth them to stray,"}, {"text": "And wander in a wilderness,"}, {"text": "wherein there is no way.", "syllables": ["wherei-", "n", "there", "is", "no", "way."]}]}, {"index": 30, "lines": [{"text": "Yet setteth he the poor on high", "bibleVerseRef": 41}, {"text": "from all his miseries,", "syllables": ["from", "all", "his", "mise-", "-", "ries,"]}, {"text": "And he, much like unto a flock,"}, {"text": "doth make him families."}]}, {"index": 31, "lines": [{"text": "They that are righteous shall rejoice,", "bibleVerseRef": 42}, {"text": "when they the same shall see;"}, {"text": "And, as ashamed, stop her mouth"}, {"text": "shall all iniquity."}]}, {"index": 32, "lines": [{"text": "Whoso is wise, and will these things", "bibleVerseRef": 43}, {"text": "observe, and them record,", "syllables": ["obser-", "ve,", "and", "them", "re-", "cord,"]}, {"text": "Ev''n they shall understand the love"}, {"text": "and kindness of the Lord."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Praise God, for he is good: for still...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (23, 'rec6742vTGywpXgUn', 119, '119:145-152 (19)', '145With my whole heart I cry''d, Lord, hear;
I will thy word obey.
146I cry''d to thee; save me, and I
will keep thy laws alway.

147I of the morning did prevent
the dawning, and did cry:
For all mine expectation
did on thy word rely.

148Mine eyes did timeously prevent
the watches of the night,
That in thy word with careful mind
then meditate I might.

149After thy loving-kindness hear
my voice, that calls on thee:
According to thy judgment, Lord,
revive and quicken me.

150Who follow mischief they draw nigh;
they from thy law are far:
151But thou art near, Lord; most firm truth
all thy commandments are.

152As for thy testimonies all,
of old this have I try''d,
That thou hast surely founded them
for ever to abide.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "With my whole heart I cry''d, Lord, hear;", "bibleVerseRef": 145}, {"text": "I will thy word obey.", "syllables": ["I", "will", "thy", "word", "obey-", "."]}, {"text": "I cry''d to thee; save me, and I", "bibleVerseRef": 146}, {"text": "will keep thy laws alway."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "I of the morning did prevent", "syllables": ["I", "of", "the", "mor-", "ning", "did", "preve-", "nt"], "bibleVerseRef": 147}, {"text": "the dawning, and did cry:"}, {"text": "For all mine expectation", "syllables": ["For", "all", "mi-", "ne", "ex-", "pec-", "ta-", "tion"]}, {"text": "did on thy word rely."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Mine eyes did timeously prevent", "bibleVerseRef": 148}, {"text": "the watches of the night,"}, {"text": "That in thy word with careful mind"}, {"text": "then meditate I might."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "After thy loving-kindness hear", "bibleVerseRef": 149}, {"text": "my voice, that calls on thee:"}, {"text": "According to thy judgment, Lord,"}, {"text": "revive and quicken me.", "syllables": ["revive", "and", "qu-", "i-", "cken", "me."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Who follow mischief they draw nigh;", "bibleVerseRef": 150}, {"text": "they from thy law are far:"}, {"text": "But thou art near, Lord; most firm truth", "bibleVerseRef": 151}, {"text": "all thy commandments are."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "As for thy testimonies all,", "bibleVerseRef": 152}, {"text": "of old this have I try''d,"}, {"text": "That thou hast surely founded them"}, {"text": "for ever to abide.", "syllables": ["for", "ever", "to", "a-", "bide-", "."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'With my whole heart I cry''d, Lord, hear...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (20, 'rec5iZXSnzKoy73TA', 50, '50 (First Version, Recommended)', '1The mighty God, the Lord,
hath spoken, and did call
The earth, from rising of the sun,
to where he hath his fall.

2From out of Sion hill,
which of excellency
And beauty the perfection is,
God shined gloriously.

3Our God shall surely come,
keep silence shall not he:
Before him fire shall waste, great storms
shall round about him be.

4Unto the heavens clear
he from above shall call,
And to the earth likewise, that he
may judge his people all.

5Together let my saints
unto me gather''d be,
Those that by sacrifice have made
a covenant with me.

6And then the heavens shall
his righteousness declare:
Because the Lord himself is he
by whom men judged are.

7My people Isr''el hear,
speak will I from on high,
Against thee I will testify;
God, ev''n thy God, am I.

8I for thy sacrifice
no blame will on thee lay,
Nor for burnt-off ''rings, which to me
thou offer''dst ev''ry day.

9I''ll take no calf nor goats
from house or fold of thine:
10For beasts of forests, cattle all
on thousand hills, are mine.

11The fowls on mountains high
are all to me well known;
Wild beasts which in the fields do lie,
ev''n they are all mine own.

12Then, if I hungry were,
I would not tell it thee;
Because the world, and fulness all
thereof, belongs to me.

13Will I eat flesh of bulls?
or goats'' blood drink will I?
14Thanks offer thou to God, and pay
thy vows to the most High.

15And call upon me when
in trouble thou shalt be;
I will deliver thee, and thou
my name shalt glorify.

16But to the wicked man
God saith, My laws and truth
Should''st thou declare? how dar''st thou take
my cov''nant in thy mouth?

17Sith thou instruction hat''st,
which should thy ways direct;
And sith my words behind thy back
thou cast''st, and dost reject.

18When thou a thief didst see,
with him thou didst consent;
And with the vile adulterers
partaker on thou went.

19Thou giv''st thy mouth to ill,
thy tongue deceit doth frame;
20Thou sitt''st, and ''gainst thy brother speak''st,
thy mother''s son dost shame.

21Because I silence kept,
while thou these things hast wrought;
That I was altogether like
thyself, hath been thy thought;

Yet I will thee reprove,
and set before thine eyes,
In order ranked, thy misdeeds
and thine iniquities.

22Now, ye that God forget,
this carefully consider;
Lest I in pieces tear you all,
and none can you deliver.

23Whoso doth offer praise
me glorifies; and I
Will shew him God''s salvation,
that orders right his way.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "The mighty God, the Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "hath spoken, and did call"}, {"text": "The earth, from rising of the sun,"}, {"text": "to where he hath his fall."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "From out of Sion hill,", "syllables": ["From", "out", "of", "Sion", "hi-", "ll,"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "which of excellency"}, {"text": "And beauty the perfection is,"}, {"text": "God shined gloriously."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Our God shall surely come,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "keep silence shall not he:"}, {"text": "Before him fire shall waste, great storms", "syllables": ["before", "him", "fire", "shall", "was-", "te,", "great", "storms"]}, {"text": "shall round about him be."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Unto the heavens clear", "syllables": ["un-", "to", "the", "heave-", "ns", "clear"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "he from above shall call,"}, {"text": "And to the earth likewise, that he"}, {"text": "may judge his people all.", "syllables": ["may", "judge", "his", "peo-", "ple", "all."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Together let my saints", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "unto me gather''d be,"}, {"text": "Those that by sacrifice have made"}, {"text": "a covenant with me.", "syllables": ["a", "cove-", "-", "nant", "with", "me."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "And then the heavens shall", "syllables": ["And", "then", "the", "heave-", "ns", "shall"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "his righteousness declare:"}, {"text": "Because the Lord himself is he"}, {"text": "by whom men judged are."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "My people Isr''el hear,", "syllables": ["My", "peo-", "ple", "is-", "r''el", "hear,"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "speak will I from on high,"}, {"text": "Against thee I will testify;"}, {"text": "God, ev''n thy God, am I."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "I for thy sacrifice", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "no blame will on thee lay,", "syllables": ["no", "blame", "will", "on", "thee", "lay,"]}, {"text": "Nor for burnt-off ''rings, which to me"}, {"text": "thou offer''dst ev''ry day."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "I''ll take no calf nor goats", "syllables": ["I''ll", "take", "no", "calf", "nor", "goats"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "from house or fold of thine:"}, {"text": "For beasts of forests, cattle all", "syllables": ["For", "beasts", "of", "fore-", "sts,", "cat-", "tle", "all"], "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "on thousand hills, are mine."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "The fowls on mountains high", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "are all to me well known;"}, {"text": "Wild beasts which in the fields do lie,"}, {"text": "ev''n they are all mine own."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Then, if I hungry were,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "I would not tell it thee;"}, {"text": "Because the world, and fulness all"}, {"text": "thereof, belongs to me."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "Will I eat flesh of bulls?", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "or goats'' blood drink will I?", "syllables": ["or", "goats''", "blood", "drink", "will", "I?"]}, {"text": "Thanks offer thou to God, and pay", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "thy vows to the most High."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "And call upon me when", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "in trouble thou shalt be;"}, {"text": "I will deliver thee, and thou", "syllables": ["I", "will", "de-", "live-", "r", "thee,", "and", "thou"]}, {"text": "my name shalt glorify."}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "But to the wicked man", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "God saith, My laws and truth"}, {"text": "Should''st thou declare? how dar''st thou take"}, {"text": "my cov''nant in thy mouth?"}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "Sith thou instruction hat''st,", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "which should thy ways direct;", "syllables": ["which", "should", "thy", "ways", "dire-", "ct;"]}, {"text": "And sith my words behind thy back"}, {"text": "thou cast''st, and dost reject."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "When thou a thief didst see,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "with him thou didst consent;"}, {"text": "And with the vile adulterers"}, {"text": "partaker on thou went.", "syllables": ["par-", "take-", "r", "on", "thou", "went."]}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "Thou giv''st thy mouth to ill,", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "thy tongue deceit doth frame;", "syllables": ["thy", "tongue", "deceit", "doth", "fra-", "me;"]}, {"text": "Thou sitt''st, and ''gainst thy brother speak''st,", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "thy mother''s son dost shame."}]}, {"index": 17, "lines": [{"text": "Because I silence kept,", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "while thou these things hast wrought;"}, {"text": "That I was altogether like"}, {"text": "thyself, hath been thy thought;", "syllables": ["thyse-", "lf,", "hath", "been", "thy", "thought;"]}]}, {"index": 18, "lines": [{"text": "Yet I will thee reprove,"}, {"text": "and set before thine eyes,"}, {"text": "In order ranked, thy misdeeds"}, {"text": "and thine iniquities."}]}, {"index": 19, "lines": [{"text": "Now, ye that God forget,", "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "this carefully consider;"}, {"text": "Lest I in pieces tear you all,", "syllables": ["Lest", "I", "in", "piece-", "s", "tear", "you", "all,"]}, {"text": "and none can you deliver.", "syllables": ["and", "none", "can", "you", "de-", "liver."]}]}, {"index": 20, "lines": [{"text": "Whoso doth offer praise", "bibleVerseRef": 23}, {"text": "me glorifies; and I"}, {"text": "Will shew him God''s salvation,", "syllables": ["Will", "shew", "him", "Go-", "d''s", "sal-", "va-", "tion,"]}, {"text": "that orders right his way."}]}]', 'SM', 'Second Version', 'The mighty God, the Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (22, 'rec65Kbq6EingIjrI', 33, '33', '1Ye righteous, in the Lord rejoice;
it comely is and right,
That upright men, with thankful voice,
should praise the Lord of might.

2Praise God with harp, and unto him
sing with the psaltery;
Upon a ten-string''d instrument
make ye sweet melody.

3A new song to him sing, and play
with loud noise skilfully;
4For right is God''s word, all his works
are done in verity.

5To judgment and to righteousness
a love he beareth still;
The loving-kindness of the Lord
the earth throughout doth fill.

6The heavens by the word of God
did their beginning take;
And by the breathing of his mouth
he all their hosts did make.

7The waters of the seas he brings
together as an heap;
And in storehouses, as it were,
he layeth up the deep.

8Let earth, and all that live therein,
with rev''rence fear the Lord;
Let all the world''s inhabitants
dread him with one accord.

9For he did speak the word, and done
it was without delay;
Established it firmly stood,
whatever he did say.

10God doth the counsel bring to nought
which heathen folk do take;
And what the people do devise
of none effect doth make.

11O but the counsel of the Lord
doth stand for ever sure;
And of his heart the purposes
from age to age endure.

12That nation blessed is, whose God
JEHOVAH is, and those
A blessed people are, whom for
his heritage he chose.

13The Lord from heav''n sees and beholds
all sons of men full well:
14He views all from his dwelling-place
that in the earth do dwell.

15He forms their hearts alike, and all
their doings he observes.
16Great hosts save not a king, much strength
no mighty man preserves.

17An horse for preservation
is a deceitful thing;
And by the greatness of his strength
can no deliv''rance bring.

18Behold on those that do him fear
the Lord doth set his eye;
Ev''n those who on his mercy do
with confidence rely.

19From death to free their soul, in dearth
life unto them to yield.
20Our soul doth wait upon the Lord;
he is our help and shield.

21Sith in his holy name we trust,
our heart shall joyful be.
22Lord, let thy mercy be on us,
as we do hope in thee.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Ye righteous, in the Lord rejoice;", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "it comely is and right,"}, {"text": "That upright men, with thankful voice,"}, {"text": "should praise the Lord of might."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Praise God with harp, and unto him", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "sing with the psaltery;"}, {"text": "Upon a ten-string''d instrument"}, {"text": "make ye sweet melody."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "A new song to him sing, and play", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "with loud noise skilfully;"}, {"text": "For right is God''s word, all his works", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "are done in verity."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "To judgment and to righteousness", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "a love he beareth still;"}, {"text": "The loving-kindness of the Lord"}, {"text": "the earth throughout doth fill."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "The heavens by the word of God", "syllables": ["The", "heave-", "ns", "by", "the", "word", "of", "God"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "did their beginning take;"}, {"text": "And by the breathing of his mouth"}, {"text": "he all their hosts did make."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "The waters of the seas he brings", "syllables": ["The", "wate-", "rs", "of", "the", "seas", "he", "brings"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "together as an heap;"}, {"text": "And in storehouses, as it were,"}, {"text": "he layeth up the deep."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Let earth, and all that live therein,", "syllables": ["Let", "earth,", "and", "all", "that", "live", "therei-", "n,"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "with rev''rence fear the Lord;"}, {"text": "Let all the world''s inhabitants"}, {"text": "dread him with one accord."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "For he did speak the word, and done", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "it was without delay;"}, {"text": "Established it firmly stood,"}, {"text": "whatever he did say.", "syllables": ["whateve-", "-", "r", "he", "did", "say."]}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "God doth the counsel bring to nought", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "which heathen folk do take;"}, {"text": "And what the people do devise", "syllables": ["And", "what", "the", "peo-", "ple", "do", "de-", "vise"]}, {"text": "of none effect doth make.", "syllables": ["of", "none", "ef-", "fect", "doth", "make."]}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "O but the counsel of the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "doth stand for ever sure;", "syllables": ["doth", "sta-", "nd", "for", "ever", "sure;"]}, {"text": "And of his heart the purposes", "syllables": ["And", "of", "his", "hea-", "rt", "the", "pur-", "poses"]}, {"text": "from age to age endure."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "That nation blessed is, whose God", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "JEHOVAH is, and those"}, {"text": "A blessed people are, whom for", "syllables": ["A", "blessed", "pe-", "o-", "ple", "are,", "whom", "for"]}, {"text": "his heritage he chose."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord from heav''n sees and beholds", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "all sons of men full well:"}, {"text": "He views all from his dwelling-place", "syllables": ["He", "views", "all", "from", "his", "dwellin-", "g-pla-", "ce"], "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "that in the earth do dwell."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "He forms their hearts alike, and all", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "their doings he observes."}, {"text": "Great hosts save not a king, much strength", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "no mighty man preserves.", "syllables": ["no", "mighty", "man", "pre-", "ser-", "ves."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "An horse for preservation", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "is a deceitful thing;"}, {"text": "And by the greatness of his strength"}, {"text": "can no deliv''rance bring.", "syllables": ["can", "no", "deliv-", "''ran-", "ce", "bring."]}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "Behold on those that do him fear", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "the Lord doth set his eye;"}, {"text": "Ev''n those who on his mercy do"}, {"text": "with confidence rely.", "syllables": ["with", "confi-", "den-", "ce", "re-", "ly."]}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "From death to free their soul, in dearth", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "life unto them to yield."}, {"text": "Our soul doth wait upon the Lord;", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "he is our help and shield."}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "Sith in his holy name we trust,", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "our heart shall joyful be."}, {"text": "Lord, let thy mercy be on us,", "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "as we do hope in thee."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Ye righteous, in the Lord rejoice...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (24, 'rec6Y72uFxjuP3Zmd', 35, '35', '1Plead, Lord, with those that plead; and fight
with those that fight with me.
2Of shield and buckler take thou hold,
stand up mine help to be.

3Draw also out the spear, and do
against them stop the way
That me pursue: unto my soul,
I''m thy salvation, say.

4Let them confounded be and sham''d
that for my soul have sought:
Who plot my hurt turn''d back be they,
and to confusion brought.

5Let them be like unto the chaff
that flies before the wind;
And let the angel of the Lord
pursue them hard behind.

6With darkness cover thou their way,
and let it slipp''ry prove;
And let the angel of the Lord
pursue them from above.

7For without cause have they for me
their net hid in a pit,
They also have without a cause
for my soul digged it.

8Let ruin seize him unawares;
his net he hid withal
Himself let catch; and in the same
destruction let him fall.

9My soul in God shall joy; and glad
in his salvation be:
10And all my bones shall say, O Lord,
who is like unto thee,

Which dost the poor set free from him
that is for him too strong;
The poor and needy from the man
that spoils and does him wrong?

11False witnesses rose; to my charge
things I not knew they laid.
12They, to the spoiling of my soul,
me ill for good repaid.

13But as for me, when they were sick,
in sackcloth sad I mourn''d:
My humbled soul did fast, my pray''r
into my bosom turn''d.

14Myself I did behave as he
had been my friend or brother;
I heavily bow''d down, as one
that mourneth for his mother.

15But in my trouble they rejoic''d,
gath''ring themselves together;
Yea, abjects vile together did
themselves against me gather:

I knew it not; they did me tear,
and quiet would not be.
16With mocking hypocrites, at feasts
they gnash''d their teeth at me.

17How long, Lord, look''st thou on? from those
destructions they intend
Rescue my soul, from lions young
my darling do defend.

18I will give thanks to thee, O Lord,
within th'' assembly great;
And where much people gather''d are
thy praises forth will set.

19Let not my wrongful enemies
proudly rejoice o''er me;
Nor who me hate without a cause,
let them wink with the eye.

20For peace they do not speak at all;
but crafty plots prepare
Against all those within the land
that meek and quiet are.

21With mouths set wide, they ''gainst me said,
Ha, ha! our eye doth see.
22Lord, thou hast seen, hold not thy peace;
Lord, be not far from me.

23Stir up thyself; wake, that thou may''st
judgment to me afford,
Ev''n to my cause, O thou that art
my only God and Lord.

24O Lord my God, do thou me judge
after thy righteousness;
And let them not their joy ''gainst me
triumphantly express:

25Nor let them say within their hearts,
Ah, we would have it thus;
Nor suffer them to say, that he
is swallow''d up by us.

26Sham''d and confounded be they all
that at my hurt are glad;
Let those against me that do boast
with shame and scorn be clad.

27Let them that love my righteous cause
be glad, shout, and not cease
To say, The Lord be magnify''d,
who loves his servant''s peace.

28Thy righteousness shall also be
declared by my tongue;
The praises that belong to thee
speak shall it all day long.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Plead, Lord, with those that plead; and fight", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "with those that fight with me."}, {"text": "Of shield and buckler take thou hold,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "stand up mine help to be."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Draw also out the spear, and do", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "against them stop the way"}, {"text": "That me pursue: unto my soul,"}, {"text": "I''m thy salvation, say."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Let them confounded be and sham''d", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "that for my soul have sought:"}, {"text": "Who plot my hurt turn''d back be they,"}, {"text": "and to confusion brought."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Let them be like unto the chaff", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "that flies before the wind;"}, {"text": "And let the angel of the Lord"}, {"text": "pursue them hard behind."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "With darkness cover thou their way,", "syllables": ["With", "dar-", "kne-", "ss", "cover", "thou", "their", "way,"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "and let it slipp''ry prove;", "syllables": ["and", "let", "it", "slipp''ry", "pro-", "ve;"]}, {"text": "And let the angel of the Lord"}, {"text": "pursue them from above."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "For without cause have they for me", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "their net hid in a pit,"}, {"text": "They also have without a cause"}, {"text": "for my soul digged it."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Let ruin seize him unawares;", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "his net he hid withal"}, {"text": "Himself let catch; and in the same"}, {"text": "destruction let him fall."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "My soul in God shall joy; and glad", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "in his salvation be:"}, {"text": "And all my bones shall say, O Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "who is like unto thee,"}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Which dost the poor set free from him"}, {"text": "that is for him too strong;"}, {"text": "The poor and needy from the man"}, {"text": "that spoils and does him wrong?"}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "False witnesses rose; to my charge", "syllables": ["false", "witnes-", "ses", "rose;", "to", "my", "char-", "ge"], "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "things I not knew they laid."}, {"text": "They, to the spoiling of my soul,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "me ill for good repaid."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "But as for me, when they were sick,", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "in sackcloth sad I mourn''d:"}, {"text": "My humbled soul did fast, my pray''r"}, {"text": "into my bosom turn''d."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "Myself I did behave as he", "syllables": ["Myse-", "lf", "I", "did", "be-", "have", "as", "he"], "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "had been my friend or brother;", "syllables": ["had", "been", "my", "friend", "or", "brother;"]}, {"text": "I heavily bow''d down, as one"}, {"text": "that mourneth for his mother.", "syllables": ["that", "mourneth", "for", "his", "mo-", "ther."]}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "But in my trouble they rejoic''d,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "gath''ring themselves together;", "syllables": ["gath''ring", "themsel-", "ves", "to-", "ge-", "ther;"]}, {"text": "Yea, abjects vile together did"}, {"text": "themselves against me gather:", "syllables": ["themselves", "a-", "gainst", "me", "ga-", "ther:"]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "I knew it not; they did me tear,"}, {"text": "and quiet would not be.", "syllables": ["and", "qui-", "et", "would", "not", "be."]}, {"text": "With mocking hypocrites, at feasts", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "they gnash''d their teeth at me."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "How long, Lord, look''st thou on? from those", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "destructions they intend"}, {"text": "Rescue my soul, from lions young", "syllables": ["res-", "cue", "my", "sou-", "l,", "from", "lions", "young"]}, {"text": "my darling do defend."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "I will give thanks to thee, O Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "within th'' assembly great;", "syllables": ["within", "th''", "as-", "sem-", "bly", "great;"]}, {"text": "And where much people gather''d are", "syllables": ["And", "where", "much", "peo-", "ple", "ga-", "ther''d", "are"]}, {"text": "thy praises forth will set.", "syllables": ["thy", "praise-", "s", "forth", "will", "set."]}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "Let not my wrongful enemies", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "proudly rejoice o''er me;"}, {"text": "Nor who me hate without a cause,"}, {"text": "let them wink with the eye."}]}, {"index": 17, "lines": [{"text": "For peace they do not speak at all;", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "but crafty plots prepare"}, {"text": "Against all those within the land"}, {"text": "that meek and quiet are.", "syllables": ["that", "meek", "and", "qui-", "et", "are."]}]}, {"index": 18, "lines": [{"text": "With mouths set wide, they ''gainst me said,", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "Ha, ha! our eye doth see."}, {"text": "Lord, thou hast seen, hold not thy peace;", "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "Lord, be not far from me."}]}, {"index": 19, "lines": [{"text": "Stir up thyself; wake, that thou may''st", "syllables": ["Stir", "up", "thyse-", "lf;", "wake,", "that", "thou", "may''st"], "bibleVerseRef": 23}, {"text": "judgment to me afford,"}, {"text": "Ev''n to my cause, O thou that art"}, {"text": "my only God and Lord."}]}, {"index": 20, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord my God, do thou me judge", "syllables": ["O", "Lord", "my", "God,", "do", "thou", "me", "judge"], "bibleVerseRef": 24}, {"text": "after thy righteousness;"}, {"text": "And let them not their joy ''gainst me"}, {"text": "triumphantly express:", "syllables": ["triu-", "m-", "phan-", "tly", "ex-", "press:"]}]}, {"index": 21, "lines": [{"text": "Nor let them say within their hearts,", "bibleVerseRef": 25}, {"tex