, "Sio-", "n,", "thine", "own", "hill:"]}, {"text": "The walls of thy Jerusalem", "syllables": ["The", "wa-", "lls", "of", "thy", "je-", "ru-", "salem"]}, {"text": "build up of thy good will.", "syllables": ["build", "up", "of", "thy", "good", "will."]}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "Then righteous off ''rings shall thee please,", "syllables": ["Then", "righteous", "off", "''rings", "shall", "thee", "plea-", "se,"], "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "and off ''rings burnt, which they"}, {"text": "With whole burnt-off ''rings,", "syllables": ["With", "who-", "le", "bur-", "nt-o-", "ff", "''ri-", "ngs,"]}, {"text": "and with calves, shall on thine altar lay.", "syllables": ["and", "with", "calves,", "shall", "on", "thinealtarlay."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'After thy loving-kindness, Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (127, 'reciMwWwJazeeAb6T', 22, '22', '1My God, my God, why hast thou me
forsaken? why so far
Art thou from helping me, and from
my words that roaring are?

2All day, my God, to thee I cry,
yet am not heard by thee;
And in the season of the night
I cannot silent be.

3But thou art holy, thou that dost
inhabit Isr''el''s praise.
4Our fathers hop''d in thee, they hop''d
and thou didst them release.

5When unto thee they sent their cry,
to them deliv''rance came:
Because they put their trust in thee,
they were not put to shame.

6But as for me, a worm I am,
and as no man am priz''d:
Reproach of men I am, and by
the people am despis''d.

7All that me see laugh me to scorn;
shoot out the lip do they;
They nod and shake their heads at me,
and, mocking, thus do say,

8This man did trust in God, that he
would free him by his might:
Let him deliver him, sith he
had in him such delight.

9But thou art he out of the womb
that didst me safely take;
When I was on my mother''s breasts
thou me to hope didst make.

10And I was cast upon thy care,
ev''n from the womb till now;
And from my mother''s belly, Lord,
my God and guide art thou.

11Be not far off, for grief is near,
and none to help is found.
12Bulls many compass me, strong bulls
of Bashan me surround.

13Their mouths they open''d wide on me,
upon me gape did they,
Like to a lion ravening
and roaring for his prey.

14Like water I''m pour''d out, my bones
all out of joint do part:
Amidst my bowels, as the wax,
so melted is my heart.

15My strength is like a potsherd dry''d;
my tongue it cleaveth fast
Unto my jaws; and to the dust
of death thou brought me hast.

16For dogs have compass''d me about:
the wicked, that did meet
In their assembly, me inclos''d;
they pierc''d my hands and feet.

17I all my bones may tell; they do
upon me look and stare.
18Upon my vesture lots they cast,
and clothes among them share.

19But be not far, O Lord, my strength;
haste to give help to me.
20From sword my soul, from pow''r of dogs
my darling set thou free.

21Out of the roaring lion''s mouth
do thou me shield and save:
For from the horns of unicorns
an ear to me thou gave.

22I will shew forth thy name unto
those that my brethren are;
Amidst the congregation
thy praise I will declare.

23Praise ye the Lord, who do him fear;
him glorify all ye
The seed of Jacob: fear him all
that Isr''el''s children be.

24For he despis''d not nor abhorr''d
th'' afflicted''s misery;
Nor from him hid his face, but heard
when he to him did cry.

25Within the congregation great
my praise shall be of thee;
My vows before them that him fear
shall be perform''d by me.

26The meek shall eat, and shall be fill''d;
they also praise shall give
Unto the Lord that do him seek:
your heart shall ever live.

27All ends of th'' earth remember shall,
and turn the Lord unto;
All kindreds of the nations
to him shall homage do:

28Because the kingdom to the Lord
doth appertain as his;
Likewise among the nations
the Governor he is.

29Earth''s fat ones eat, and worship shall:
all who to dust descend
Shall bow to him; none of them can
his soul from death defend.

30A seed shall service do to him;
unto the Lord it shall
Be for a generation
reckon''d in ages all.

31They shall come, and they shall declare
his truth and righteousness
Unto a people yet unborn,
and that he hath done this.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "My God, my God, why hast thou me", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "forsaken? why so far", "syllables": ["for-", "sake-", "n?", "why", "so", "far"]}, {"text": "Art thou from helping me, and from"}, {"text": "my words that roaring are?", "syllables": ["my", "words", "that", "roa-", "ring", "are?"]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "All day, my God, to thee I cry,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "yet am not heard by thee;"}, {"text": "And in the season of the night"}, {"text": "I cannot silent be.", "syllables": ["I", "can-", "not", "sile-", "nt", "be."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "But thou art holy, thou that dost", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "inhabit Isr''el''s praise."}, {"text": "Our fathers hop''d in thee, they hop''d", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "and thou didst them release."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "When unto thee they sent their cry,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "to them deliv''rance came:", "syllables": ["to", "them", "deliv-", "''ran-", "ce", "came:"]}, {"text": "Because they put their trust in thee,"}, {"text": "they were not put to shame."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "But as for me, a worm I am,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "and as no man am priz''d:"}, {"text": "Reproach of men I am, and by", "syllables": ["repro-", "ach", "of", "men", "I", "am,", "and", "by"]}, {"text": "the people am despis''d.", "syllables": ["the", "peo-", "ple", "am", "des-", "pis''d."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "All that me see laugh me to scorn;", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "shoot out the lip do they;"}, {"text": "They nod and shake their heads at me,"}, {"text": "and, mocking, thus do say,"}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "This man did trust in God, that he", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "would free him by his might:"}, {"text": "Let him deliver him, sith he", "syllables": ["Let", "him", "de-", "live-", "r", "him,", "sith", "he"]}, {"text": "had in him such delight."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "But thou art he out of the womb", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "that didst me safely take;"}, {"text": "When I was on my mother''s breasts"}, {"text": "thou me to hope didst make."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "And I was cast upon thy care,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "ev''n from the womb till now;"}, {"text": "And from my mother''s belly, Lord,"}, {"text": "my God and guide art thou.", "syllables": ["my", "God", "and", "guide", "art", "thou."]}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "Be not far off, for grief is near,", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "and none to help is found.", "syllables": ["and", "none", "to", "help", "is", "found."]}, {"text": "Bulls many compass me, strong bulls", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "of Bashan me surround."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Their mouths they open''d wide on me,", "syllables": ["Their", "mou-", "ths", "they", "open''d", "wide", "on", "me,"], "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "upon me gape did they,"}, {"text": "Like to a lion ravening", "syllables": ["Like", "to", "a", "lion", "rave-", "-", "-", "ning"]}, {"text": "and roaring for his prey.", "syllables": ["and", "roa-", "ring", "for", "his", "prey."]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "Like water I''m pour''d out, my bones", "syllables": ["Like", "water", "I''m", "pou-", "r''d", "out,", "my", "bones"], "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "all out of joint do part:"}, {"text": "Amidst my bowels, as the wax,", "syllables": ["a-", "midst", "my", "bowe-", "ls,", "as", "the", "wax,"]}, {"text": "so melted is my heart."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "My strength is like a potsherd dry''d;", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "my tongue it cleaveth fast", "syllables": ["my", "tongue", "it", "clea-", "veth", "fast"]}, {"text": "Unto my jaws; and to the dust"}, {"text": "of death thou brought me hast."}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "For dogs have compass''d me about:", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "the wicked, that did meet"}, {"text": "In their assembly, me inclos''d;"}, {"text": "they pierc''d my hands and feet."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "I all my bones may tell; they do", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "upon me look and stare.", "syllables": ["upon", "me", "look", "and", "sta-", "re."]}, {"text": "Upon my vesture lots they cast,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "and clothes among them share.", "syllables": ["and", "clothes", "a-", "mong", "them", "share."]}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "But be not far, O Lord, my strength;", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "haste to give help to me.", "syllables": ["haste", "to", "give", "help", "to", "me."]}, {"text": "From sword my soul, from pow''r of dogs", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "my darling set thou free."}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "Out of the roaring lion''s mouth", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "do thou me shield and save:"}, {"text": "For from the horns of unicorns"}, {"text": "an ear to me thou gave."}]}, {"index": 17, "lines": [{"text": "I will shew forth thy name unto", "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "those that my brethren are;"}, {"text": "Amidst the congregation", "syllables": ["a-", "mi-", "dst", "the", "con-", "gre-", "ga-", "tion"]}, {"text": "thy praise I will declare."}]}, {"index": 18, "lines": [{"text": "Praise ye the Lord, who do him fear;", "bibleVerseRef": 23}, {"text": "him glorify all ye"}, {"text": "The seed of Jacob: fear him all"}, {"text": "that Isr''el''s children be."}]}, {"index": 19, "lines": [{"text": "For he despis''d not nor abhorr''d", "bibleVerseRef": 24}, {"text": "th'' afflicted''s misery;"}, {"text": "Nor from him hid his face, but heard"}, {"text": "when he to him did cry."}]}, {"index": 20, "lines": [{"text": "Within the congregation great", "bibleVerseRef": 25}, {"text": "my praise shall be of thee;"}, {"text": "My vows before them that him fear"}, {"text": "shall be perform''d by me."}]}, {"index": 21, "lines": [{"text": "The meek shall eat, and shall be fill''d;", "bibleVerseRef": 26}, {"text": "they also praise shall give"}, {"text": "Unto the Lord that do him seek:"}, {"text": "your heart shall ever live.", "syllables": ["your", "hea-", "rt", "shall", "ever", "live."]}]}, {"index": 22, "lines": [{"text": "All ends of th'' earth remember shall,", "syllables": ["All", "ends", "of", "th''", "earth", "remem-", "ber", "shall,"], "bibleVerseRef": 27}, {"text": "and turn the Lord unto;"}, {"text": "All kindreds of the nations", "syllables": ["All", "kin-", "dre-", "ds", "of", "the", "na-", "tions"]}, {"text": "to him shall homage do:"}]}, {"index": 23, "lines": [{"text": "Because the kingdom to the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 28}, {"text": "doth appertain as his;"}, {"text": "Likewise among the nations", "syllables": ["like-", "-", "wise", "a-", "mong", "the", "na-", "tions"]}, {"text": "the Governor he is.", "syllables": ["the", "gove-", "r-", "nor", "he", "is."]}]}, {"index": 24, "lines": [{"text": "Earth''s fat ones eat, and worship shall:", "bibleVerseRef": 29}, {"text": "all who to dust descend"}, {"text": "Shall bow to him; none of them can", "syllables": ["Shall", "bow", "to", "him;", "none", "of", "them", "can"]}, {"text": "his soul from death defend."}]}, {"index": 25, "lines": [{"text": "A seed shall service do to him;", "bibleVerseRef": 30}, {"text": "unto the Lord it shall"}, {"text": "Be for a generation", "syllables": ["Be", "for", "a", "ge-", "ne-", "ra-", "tio-", "n"]}, {"text": "reckon''d in ages all.", "syllables": ["rec-", "ko-", "n''d", "in", "ages", "all."]}]}, {"index": 26, "lines": [{"text": "They shall come, and they shall declare", "bibleVerseRef": 31}, {"text": "his truth and righteousness"}, {"text": "Unto a people yet unborn,", "syllables": ["unto", "a", "pe-", "o-", "ple", "yet", "un-", "born,"]}, {"text": "and that he hath done this."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'My God, my God, why hast thou me...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (123, 'rechUYgxlSGMx7gxn', 129, '129', '1Oft did they vex me from my youth,
may Isr''el now declare;
2Oft did they vex me from my youth,
yet not victorious were.

3The plowers plow''d upon my back;
they long their furrows drew.
4The righteous Lord did cut the cords
of the ungodly crew.

5Let Sion''s haters all be turn''d
back with confusion.
6As grass on houses'' tops be they,
which fades ere it be grown:

7Whereof enough to fill his hand
the mower cannot find;
Nor can the man his bosom fill,
whose work is sheaves to bind.

8Neither say they who do go by,
God''s blessing on you rest:
We in the name of God
the Lord do wish you to be blest.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Oft did they vex me from my youth,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "may Isr''el now declare;"}, {"text": "Oft did they vex me from my youth,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "yet not victorious were."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The plowers plow''d upon my back;", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "they long their furrows drew."}, {"text": "The righteous Lord did cut the cords", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "of the ungodly crew."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Let Sion''s haters all be turn''d", "syllables": ["Let", "Sio-", "n''s", "hate-", "rs", "all", "be", "turn''d"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "back with confusion.", "syllables": ["back", "with", "con-", "fu-", "sio-", "n."]}, {"text": "As grass on houses'' tops be they,", "syllables": ["As", "grass", "on", "house-", "s''", "tops", "be", "they,"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "which fades ere it be grown:"}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Whereof enough to fill his hand", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "the mower cannot find;", "syllables": ["the", "mowe-", "r", "can-", "not", "find;"]}, {"text": "Nor can the man his bosom fill,"}, {"text": "whose work is sheaves to bind."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Neither say they who do go by,", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "God''s blessing on you rest:"}, {"text": "We in the name of God", "syllables": ["We", "in", "the", "na-", "-", "me", "of", "God"]}, {"text": "the Lord do wish you to be blest.", "syllables": ["the", "Lord", "do", "wish", "you", "tobeblest."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Oft did they vex me from my youth...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (131, 'recjAA8Q5KGvREPmd', 84, '84', '1How lovely is thy dwelling-place,
O Lord of hosts, to me!
The tabernacles of thy grace
how pleasant, Lord, they be!

2My thirsty soul longs veh''mently,
yea faints, thy courts to see:
My very heart and flesh cry out,
O living God, for thee.

3Behold, the sparrow findeth out
an house wherein to rest;
The swallow also for herself
hath purchased a nest;

Ev''n thine own altars, where she safe
her young ones forth may bring,
O thou almighty Lord of hosts,
who art my God and King.

4Bless''d are they in thy house that dwell,
they ever give thee praise.
5Bless''d is the man whose strength thou art,
in whose heart are thy ways:

6Who passing thorough Baca''s vale,
therein do dig up wells;
Also the rain that falleth down
the pools with water fills.

7So they from strength unwearied go
still forward unto strength,
Until in Sion they appear
before the Lord at length.

8Lord God of hosts, my prayer hear;
O Jacob''s God, give ear.
9See God our shield, look on the face
of thine anointed dear.

10For in thy courts one day excels
a thousand; rather in
My God''s house will I keep a door,
than dwell in tents of sin.

11For God the Lord''s a sun and shield:
he''ll grace and glory give;
And will withhold no good from them
that uprightly do live.

12O thou that art the Lord of hosts,
that man is truly blest,
Who by assured confidence
on thee alone doth rest.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "How lovely is thy dwelling-place,", "syllables": ["How", "lovely", "is", "thy", "dwel-", "lin-", "g-pla-", "ce,"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "O Lord of hosts, to me!"}, {"text": "The tabernacles of thy grace"}, {"text": "how pleasant, Lord, they be!"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "My thirsty soul longs veh''mently,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "yea faints, thy courts to see:"}, {"text": "My very heart and flesh cry out,"}, {"text": "O living God, for thee."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Behold, the sparrow findeth out", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "an house wherein to rest;", "syllables": ["an", "house", "wherei-", "n", "to", "rest;"]}, {"text": "The swallow also for herself"}, {"text": "hath purchased a nest;"}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Ev''n thine own altars, where she safe"}, {"text": "her young ones forth may bring,"}, {"text": "O thou almighty Lord of hosts,"}, {"text": "who art my God and King."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Bless''d are they in thy house that dwell,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "they ever give thee praise.", "syllables": ["they", "ever", "give", "thee", "praise-", "."]}, {"text": "Bless''d is the man whose strength thou art,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "in whose heart are thy ways:"}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Who passing thorough Baca''s vale,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "therein do dig up wells;", "syllables": ["therei-", "n", "do", "dig", "up", "wells;"]}, {"text": "Also the rain that falleth down"}, {"text": "the pools with water fills.", "syllables": ["the", "pools", "with", "water", "fi-", "lls."]}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "So they from strength unwearied go", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "still forward unto strength,"}, {"text": "Until in Sion they appear", "syllables": ["un-", "til", "in", "Sio-", "n", "they", "ap-", "pear"]}, {"text": "before the Lord at length."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "Lord God of hosts, my prayer hear;", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "O Jacob''s God, give ear."}, {"text": "See God our shield, look on the face", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "of thine anointed dear."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "For in thy courts one day excels", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "a thousand; rather in"}, {"text": "My God''s house will I keep a door,"}, {"text": "than dwell in tents of sin."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "For God the Lord''s a sun and shield:", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "he''ll grace and glory give;", "syllables": ["he''ll", "grace", "and", "glo-", "ry", "give;"]}, {"text": "And will withhold no good from them"}, {"text": "that uprightly do live."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "O thou that art the Lord of hosts,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "that man is truly blest,"}, {"text": "Who by assured confidence", "syllables": ["Who", "by", "assu-", "red", "con-", "fi-", "den-", "ce"]}, {"text": "on thee alone doth rest."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'How lovely is thy dwelling-place...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (132, 'recjzFxiVASY35X7Q', 98, '98', '1O sing a new song to the Lord,
for wonders he hath done:
His right hand and his holy arm
him victory hath won.

2The Lord God his salvation
hath caused to be known;
His justice in the heathen''s sight
he openly hath shown.

3He mindful of his grace and truth
to Isr''el''s house hath been;
And the salvation of our God
all ends of th'' earth have seen.

4Let all the earth unto the Lord
send forth a joyful noise;
Lift up your voice aloud to him,
sing praises, and rejoice.

5With harp, with harp, and voice of psalms,
unto JEHOVAH sing:
6With trumpets, cornets, gladly sound
before the Lord the King.

7Let seas and all their fulness roar;
the world, and dwellers there;
8Let floods clap hands, and let the hills
together joy declare

9Before the Lord; because he comes,
to judge the earth comes he:
He''ll judge the world with righteousness,
his folk with equity.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "O sing a new song to the Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "for wonders he hath done:"}, {"text": "His right hand and his holy arm"}, {"text": "him victory hath won."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord God his salvation", "syllables": ["The", "Lo-", "rd", "God", "his", "sal-", "va-", "tion"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "hath caused to be known;"}, {"text": "His justice in the heathen''s sight"}, {"text": "he openly hath shown.", "syllables": ["he", "open-", "ly", "hath", "sho-", "wn."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "He mindful of his grace and truth", "syllables": ["He", "mindful", "of", "his", "gra-", "ce", "and", "truth"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "to Isr''el''s house hath been;"}, {"text": "And the salvation of our God"}, {"text": "all ends of th'' earth have seen.", "syllables": ["all", "ends", "of", "th''", "earth", "haveseen."]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Let all the earth unto the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "send forth a joyful noise;"}, {"text": "Lift up your voice aloud to him,"}, {"text": "sing praises, and rejoice.", "syllables": ["sing", "praise-", "s,", "and", "re-", "joice."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "With harp, with harp, and voice of psalms,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "unto JEHOVAH sing:"}, {"text": "With trumpets, cornets, gladly sound", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "before the Lord the King."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Let seas and all their fulness roar;", "syllables": ["Let", "seas", "and", "all", "their", "fulness", "ro-", "ar;"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "the world, and dwellers there;"}, {"text": "Let floods clap hands, and let the hills", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "together joy declare"}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Before the Lord; because he comes,", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "to judge the earth comes he:", "syllables": ["to", "judge", "the", "earth", "comes", "he:"]}, {"text": "He''ll judge the world with righteousness,", "syllables": ["He''ll", "judge", "the", "world", "with", "righ-", "teous-", "ness,"]}, {"text": "his folk with equity.", "syllables": ["his", "folk", "with", "equ-", "i-", "ty."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'O sing a new song to the Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (149, 'recoACD4AGLfY9kIx', 1, '1', '1That man hath perfect blessedness,
who walketh not astray
In counsel of ungodly men,
nor stands in sinners'' way,

Nor sitteth in the scorner''s chair:
2But placeth his delight
Upon God''s law, and meditates
on his law day and night.

3He shall be like a tree that grows
near planted by a river,
Which in his season yields his fruit,
and his leaf fadeth never:

And all he doth shall prosper well
4The wicked are not so;
But like they are unto the chaff,
which wind drives to and fro.

5In judgment therefore shall not stand
such as ungodly are;
Nor in th'' assembly of the just
shall wicked men appear.

6For why? the way of godly men
unto the Lord is known:
Whereas the way of wicked men
shall quite be overthrown.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "That man hath perfect blessedness,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "who walketh not astray"}, {"text": "In counsel of ungodly men,"}, {"text": "nor stands in sinners'' way,"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Nor sitteth in the scorner''s chair:"}, {"text": "But placeth his delight", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "Upon God''s law, and meditates", "syllables": ["upon", "God''s", "law,", "and", "me-", "di-", "ta-", "tes"]}, {"text": "on his law day and night."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "He shall be like a tree that grows", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "near planted by a river,"}, {"text": "Which in his season yields his fruit,", "syllables": ["Which", "in", "his", "season", "yields", "his", "fru-", "it,"]}, {"text": "and his leaf fadeth never:", "syllables": ["and", "his", "leaf", "fadeeth", "ne-", "ver:"]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "And all he doth shall prosper well"}, {"text": "The wicked are not so;", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "But like they are unto the chaff,"}, {"text": "which wind drives to and fro.", "syllables": ["which", "wind", "drives", "to", "and", "fro."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "In judgment therefore shall not stand", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "such as ungodly are;"}, {"text": "Nor in th'' assembly of the just", "syllables": ["Nor", "in", "th''", "assem-", "bly", "of", "the", "just"]}, {"text": "shall wicked men appear."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "For why? the way of godly men", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "unto the Lord is known:"}, {"text": "Whereas the way of wicked men", "syllables": ["Wherea-", "s", "the", "way", "of", "wic-", "ked", "men"]}, {"text": "shall quite be overthrown.", "syllables": ["shall", "qui-", "te", "be", "over-", "thrown."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'That man hath perfect blessedness...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (138, 'reclTQva6yvJBnryi', 124, '124 (Second Version, Recommended)', '1Now Israel
may say, and that truly,
If that the Lord
had not our cause maintain''d;

2If that the Lord
had not our right sustain''d,
When cruel men
against us furiously

Rose up in wrath,
to make of us their prey;
3Then certainly
they had devour''d us all,

And swallow''d quick,
for ought that we could deem;
Such was their rage,
as we might well esteem.

4And as fierce floods
before them all things drown,
So had they brought
our soul to death quite down.

5The raging streams,
with their proud swelling waves,
Had then our soul
o''erwhelmed in the deep.

6But bless''d be God,
who doth us safely keep,
And hath not giv''n
us for a living prey

Unto their teeth,
and bloody cruelty.
7Ev''n as a bird
out of the fowler''s snare

Escapes away,
so is our soul set free;
Broke are their nets,
and thus escaped we.

8Therefore our help
is in the Lord''s great name,
Who heav''n and earth
by his great pow''r did frame.', NULL, '10 10 10 10 10', 'Second Version', 'Now Israel...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (130, 'recj24AeQGQaO7roT', 25, '25 (First Version, Recommended)', '1To thee I lift my soul:
2O Lord, I trust in thee:
My God, let me not be asham''d,
nor foes triumph o''er me.

3Let none that wait on thee
be put to shame at all;
But those that without cause transgress,
let shame upon them fall.

4Shew me thy ways, O Lord;
thy paths, O teach thou me:
5And do thou lead me in thy truth,
therein my teacher be:

For thou art God that dost
to me salvation send,
And I upon thee all the day
expecting do attend.

6Thy tender mercies, Lord,
I pray thee to remember,
And loving-kindnesses; for they
have been of old for ever.

7My sins and faults of youth
do thou, O Lord, forget:
After thy mercy think on me,
and for thy goodness great.

8God good and upright is:
the way he''ll sinners show.
9The meek in judgment he will guide,
and make his path to know.

10The whole paths of the Lord
are truth and mercy sure,
To those that do his cov''nant keep,
and testimonies pure.

11Now, for thine own name''s sake,
O Lord, I thee entreat
To pardon mine iniquity;
for it is very great.

12What man is he that fears
the Lord, and doth him serve?
Him shall he teach the way that he
shall choose, and still observe.

13His soul shall dwell at ease;
and his posterity
Shall flourish still, and of the earth
inheritors shall be.

14With those that fear him is
the secret of the Lord;
The knowledge of his covenant
he will to them afford.

15Mine eyes upon the Lord
continually are set:
For he it is that shall bring forth
my feet out of the net.

16Turn unto me thy face,
and to me mercy show;
Because that I am desolate,
and am brought very low.

17My heart''s griefs are increas''d:
me from distress relieve.
18See mine affliction and my pain,
and all my sins forgive.

19Consider thou my foes,
because they many are;
And it a cruel hatred is
which they against me bear.

20O do thou keep my soul,
do thou deliver me:
And let me never be asham''d,
because I trust in thee.

21Let uprightness and truth
keep me, who thee attend.
22Redemption, Lord, to Israel
from all his troubles send.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "To thee I lift my soul:", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "O Lord, I trust in thee:", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "My God, let me not be asham''d,"}, {"text": "nor foes triumph o''er me.", "syllables": ["nor", "foes", "triu-", "mph", "o''er", "me."]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Let none that wait on thee", "syllables": ["Let", "none", "that", "wait", "on", "thee"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "be put to shame at all;"}, {"text": "But those that without cause transgress,"}, {"text": "let shame upon them fall."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Shew me thy ways, O Lord;", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "thy paths, O teach thou me:"}, {"text": "And do thou lead me in thy truth,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "therein my teacher be:", "syllables": ["therei-", "n", "my", "tea-", "cher", "be:"]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "For thou art God that dost"}, {"text": "to me salvation send,"}, {"text": "And I upon thee all the day"}, {"text": "expecting do attend."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Thy tender mercies, Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "I pray thee to remember,", "syllables": ["I", "pray", "thee", "to", "remem-", "ber,"]}, {"text": "And loving-kindnesses; for they"}, {"text": "have been of old for ever."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "My sins and faults of youth", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "do thou, O Lord, forget:"}, {"text": "After thy mercy think on me,"}, {"text": "and for thy goodness great."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "God good and upright is:", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "the way he''ll sinners show."}, {"text": "The meek in judgment he will guide,", "syllables": ["The", "meek", "in", "judgment", "he", "will", "gui-", "de,"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "and make his path to know."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "The whole paths of the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "are truth and mercy sure,"}, {"text": "To those that do his cov''nant keep,"}, {"text": "and testimonies pure."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Now, for thine own name''s sake,", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "O Lord, I thee entreat"}, {"text": "To pardon mine iniquity;"}, {"text": "for it is very great."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "What man is he that fears", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "the Lord, and doth him serve?"}, {"text": "Him shall he teach the way that he"}, {"text": "shall choose, and still observe.", "syllables": ["shall", "choose,", "and", "still", "obser-", "ve."]}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "His soul shall dwell at ease;", "syllables": ["His", "soul", "shall", "dwell", "at", "ease;"], "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "and his posterity"}, {"text": "Shall flourish still, and of the earth"}, {"text": "inheritors shall be."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "With those that fear him is", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "the secret of the Lord;"}, {"text": "The knowledge of his covenant"}, {"text": "he will to them afford."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "Mine eyes upon the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "continually are set:", "syllables": ["conti-", "nu-", "a-", "lly", "are", "set:"]}, {"text": "For he it is that shall bring forth"}, {"text": "my feet out of the net."}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "Turn unto me thy face,", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "and to me mercy show;"}, {"text": "Because that I am desolate,"}, {"text": "and am brought very low."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "My heart''s griefs are increas''d:", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "me from distress relieve."}, {"text": "See mine affliction and my pain,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "and all my sins forgive."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "Consider thou my foes,", "syllables": ["con-", "side-", "r", "thou", "my", "foes,"], "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "because they many are;"}, {"text": "And it a cruel hatred is", "syllables": ["And", "it", "a", "crue-", "l", "hat-", "red", "is"]}