", "bibleVerseRef": 37}, {"text": "weak in their tribes were none.", "syllables": ["weak", "in", "their", "tribes", "were", "none."]}]}, {"index": 28, "lines": [{"text": "Egypt was glad when forth they went,", "bibleVerseRef": 38}, {"text": "their fear on them did light."}, {"text": "He spread a cloud for covering,", "syllables": ["He", "sprea-", "d", "a", "cloud", "for", "cove-", "ring,"], "bibleVerseRef": 39}, {"text": "and fire to shine by night."}]}, {"index": 29, "lines": [{"text": "They ask''d, and he brought quails:", "bibleVerseRef": 40}, {"text": "with bread of heav''n he filled them.", "syllables": ["with", "bread", "of", "heav''n", "he", "filledthem."]}, {"text": "He open''d rocks, floods gush''d,", "syllables": ["He", "ope-", "n''d", "ro-", "cks,", "floods", "gu-", "sh''d,"], "bibleVerseRef": 41}, {"text": "and ran in deserts like a stream.", "syllables": ["and", "ran", "in", "deserts", "like", "astream."]}]}, {"index": 30, "lines": [{"text": "For on his holy promise he,", "bibleVerseRef": 42}, {"text": "and servant Abr''ham, thought."}, {"text": "With joy his people, his elect", "bibleVerseRef": 43}, {"text": "with gladness, forth he brought."}]}, {"index": 31, "lines": [{"text": "And unto them the pleasant lands", "bibleVerseRef": 44}, {"text": "he of the heathen gave;"}, {"text": "That of the people''s labour they", "syllables": ["That", "of", "the", "peo-", "ple''s", "la-", "bour", "they"]}, {"text": "inheritance might have.", "syllables": ["inhe-", "ri-", "tan-", "ce", "might", "have."]}]}, {"index": 32, "lines": [{"text": "That they his statutes might observe", "syllables": ["That", "they", "his", "statutes", "might", "ob-", "ser-", "ve"], "bibleVerseRef": 45}, {"text": "according to his word;"}, {"text": "And that they might his laws obey.", "syllables": ["And", "that", "they", "mi-", "ght", "his", "laws", "obey."]}, {"text": "Give praise unto the Lord."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Give thanks to God, call on his name...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (172, 'recvwj1mCGen5qrKu', 28, '28', '1To thee I''ll cry, O Lord, my rock;
hold not thy peace to me;
Lest like those that to pit descend
I by thy silence be.

2The voice hear of my humble pray''rs,
when unto thee I cry;
When to thine holy oracle
I lift mine hands on high.

3With ill men draw me not away
that work iniquity;
That speak peace to their friends, while in
their hearts doth mischief lie.

4Give them according to their deeds
and ills endeavoured:
And as their handy-works deserve,
to them be rendered.

5God shall not build, but them destroy,
who would not understand
The Lord''s own works, nor did regard
the doing of his hand.

6For ever blessed be the Lord,
for graciously he heard
The voice of my petitions,
and prayers did regard.

7The Lord''s my strength and shield; my heart
upon him did rely;
And I am helped: hence my heart
doth joy exceedingly,

And with my song I will him praise.
8Their strength is God alone:
He also is the saving strength
of his anointed one.

9O thine own people do thou save,
bless thine inheritance;
Them also do thou feed, and them
for evermore advance.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "To thee I''ll cry, O Lord, my rock;", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "hold not thy peace to me;"}, {"text": "Lest like those that to pit descend"}, {"text": "I by thy silence be."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The voice hear of my humble pray''rs,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "when unto thee I cry;"}, {"text": "When to thine holy oracle"}, {"text": "I lift mine hands on high."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "With ill men draw me not away", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "that work iniquity;"}, {"text": "That speak peace to their friends, while in"}, {"text": "their hearts doth mischief lie."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Give them according to their deeds", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "and ills endeavoured:"}, {"text": "And as their handy-works deserve,"}, {"text": "to them be rendered."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "God shall not build, but them destroy,", "syllables": ["God", "shall", "not", "build,", "but", "them", "des-", "troy,"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "who would not understand"}, {"text": "The Lord''s own works, nor did regard"}, {"text": "the doing of his hand.", "syllables": ["the", "doi-", "ng", "of", "his", "hand."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "For ever blessed be the Lord,", "syllables": ["For", "ever", "ble-", "s-", "sed", "be", "the", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "for graciously he heard"}, {"text": "The voice of my petitions,", "syllables": ["The", "voice", "of", "my", "pe-", "ti-", "tio-", "ns,"]}, {"text": "and prayers did regard."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord''s my strength and shield; my heart", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "upon him did rely;"}, {"text": "And I am helped: hence my heart"}, {"text": "doth joy exceedingly,"}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "And with my song I will him praise."}, {"text": "Their strength is God alone:", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "He also is the saving strength"}, {"text": "of his anointed one."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "O thine own people do thou save,", "syllables": ["O", "thine", "own", "peo-", "ple", "do", "thou", "save,"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "bless thine inheritance;", "syllables": ["bless", "thine", "inhe-", "ri-", "tan-", "ce;"]}, {"text": "Them also do thou feed, and them"}, {"text": "for evermore advance."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'To thee I''ll cry, O Lord, my rock...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (170, 'recv93wiu9MyvIOGa', 86, '86', '1O Lord, do thou bow down thine ear,
and hear me graciously;
Because I sore afflicted am,
and am in poverty.

2Because I''m holy, let my soul
by thee preserved be:
O thou my God, thy servant save,
that puts his trust in thee.

3Sith unto thee I daily cry,
be merciful to me.
4Rejoice thy servant''s soul; for, Lord,
I lift my soul to thee.

5For thou art gracious, O Lord,
and ready to forgive;
And rich in mercy, all that call
upon thee to relieve.

6Hear, Lord, my pray''r; unto the voice
of my request attend:
7In troublous times I''ll call on thee;
for thou wilt answer send.

8Lord, there is none among the gods
that may with thee compare;
And like the works which thou hast done,
not any work is there.

9All nations whom thou mad''st shall come
and worship rev''rently
Before thy face; and they, O Lord,
thy name shall glorify.

10Because thou art exceeding great,
and works by thee are done
Which are to be admir''d; and thou
art God thyself alone.

11Teach me thy way, and in thy truth,
O Lord, then walk will I;
Unite my heart, that I thy name
may fear continually.

12O Lord my God, with all my heart
to thee I will give praise;
And I the glory will ascribe
unto thy name always:

13Because thy mercy toward me
in greatness doth excel;
And thou deliver''d hast my soul
out from the lowest hell.

14O God, the proud against me rise,
and vi''lent men have met,
That for my soul have sought; and thee
before them have not set.

15But thou art full of pity, Lord,
a God most gracious,
Long-suffering, and in thy truth
and mercy plenteous.

16O turn to me thy countenance,
and mercy on me have;
Thy servant strengthen, and the son
of thine own handmaid save.

17Shew me a sign for good, that they
which do me hate may see,
And be asham''d; because thou, Lord,
didst help and comfort me.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord, do thou bow down thine ear,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "and hear me graciously;"}, {"text": "Because I sore afflicted am,"}, {"text": "and am in poverty.", "syllables": ["and", "am", "in", "pove-", "r-", "ty."]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Because I''m holy, let my soul", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "by thee preserved be:"}, {"text": "O thou my God, thy servant save,"}, {"text": "that puts his trust in thee."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Sith unto thee I daily cry,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "be merciful to me."}, {"text": "Rejoice thy servant''s soul; for, Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "I lift my soul to thee."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "For thou art gracious, O Lord,", "syllables": ["For", "thou", "art", "gra-", "ciou-", "s,", "O", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "and ready to forgive;"}, {"text": "And rich in mercy, all that call"}, {"text": "upon thee to relieve."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Hear, Lord, my pray''r; unto the voice", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "of my request attend:"}, {"text": "In troublous times I''ll call on thee;", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "for thou wilt answer send."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, there is none among the gods", "syllables": ["Lord,", "there", "is", "none", "a-", "mong", "the", "gods"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "that may with thee compare;"}, {"text": "And like the works which thou hast done,"}, {"text": "not any work is there."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "All nations whom thou mad''st shall come", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "and worship rev''rently"}, {"text": "Before thy face; and they, O Lord,"}, {"text": "thy name shall glorify."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "Because thou art exceeding great,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "and works by thee are done"}, {"text": "Which are to be admir''d; and thou"}, {"text": "art God thyself alone.", "syllables": ["art", "God", "thyse-", "lf", "a-", "lone."]}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Teach me thy way, and in thy truth,", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "O Lord, then walk will I;"}, {"text": "Unite my heart, that I thy name"}, {"text": "may fear continually.", "syllables": ["may", "fear", "conti-", "nu-", "a-", "lly."]}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord my God, with all my heart", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "to thee I will give praise;"}, {"text": "And I the glory will ascribe", "syllables": ["And", "I", "the", "glory", "will", "as-", "cri-", "be"]}, {"text": "unto thy name always:"}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Because thy mercy toward me", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "in greatness doth excel;"}, {"text": "And thou deliver''d hast my soul"}, {"text": "out from the lowest hell.", "syllables": ["out", "from", "the", "lowe-", "st", "hell."]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "O God, the proud against me rise,", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "and vi''lent men have met,"}, {"text": "That for my soul have sought; and thee"}, {"text": "before them have not set."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "But thou art full of pity, Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "a God most gracious,", "syllables": ["a", "God", "most", "gra-", "ciou-", "s,"]}, {"text": "Long-suffering, and in thy truth"}, {"text": "and mercy plenteous.", "syllables": ["and", "mercy", "plen-", "te-", "o-", "us."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "O turn to me thy countenance,", "syllables": ["O", "turn", "to", "me", "thy", "counte-", "nan-", "ce,"], "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "and mercy on me have;"}, {"text": "Thy servant strengthen, and the son"}, {"text": "of thine own handmaid save."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "Shew me a sign for good, that they", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "which do me hate may see,"}, {"text": "And be asham''d; because thou, Lord,"}, {"text": "didst help and comfort me."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'O Lord, do thou bow down thine ear...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (177, 'recxIkLHZvPeFisIA', 123, '123', '1O thou that dwellest in the heav''ns,
I lift mine eyes to thee.
2Behold, as servants'' eyes do look
their masters'' hand to see,

As handmaid''s eyes her mistress'' hand;
so do our eyes attend
Upon the Lord our God, until
to us he mercy send.

3O Lord, be gracious to us,
unto us gracious be;
Because replenish''d with contempt
exceedingly are we.

4Our soul is fill''d with scorn of those
that at their ease abide,
And with the insolent contempt
of those that swell in pride.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "O thou that dwellest in the heav''ns,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "I lift mine eyes to thee."}, {"text": "Behold, as servants'' eyes do look", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "their masters'' hand to see,"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "As handmaid''s eyes her mistress'' hand;"}, {"text": "so do our eyes attend"}, {"text": "Upon the Lord our God, until"}, {"text": "to us he mercy send."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord, be gracious to us,", "syllables": ["O", "Lo-", "rd,", "be", "gra-", "cious", "to", "us,"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "unto us gracious be;"}, {"text": "Because replenish''d with contempt"}, {"text": "exceedingly are we."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Our soul is fill''d with scorn of those", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "that at their ease abide,", "syllables": ["that", "at", "their", "ease", "a-", "bide,"]}, {"text": "And with the insolent contempt"}, {"text": "of those that swell in pride.", "syllables": ["of", "those", "that", "swell", "in", "pride."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'O thou that dwellest in the heav''ns...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (179, 'recxcWUcMeFHEdnKV', 119, '119:137-144 (18)', '139My zeal hath ev''n consumed me,
because mine enemies
Thy holy words forgotten have,
and do thy laws despise.

140Thy word''s most pure, therefore on it
thy servant''s love is set.
141Small, and despis''d I am, yet I
thy precepts not forget.

142Thy righteousness is righteousness
which ever doth endure:
Thy holy law, Lord, also is
the very truth most pure.

143Trouble and anguish have me found,
and taken hold on me:
Yet in my trouble my delight
thy just commandments be.

144Eternal righteousness is in
thy testimonies all:
Lord, to me understanding give,
and ever live I shall.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "My zeal hath ev''n consumed me,", "bibleVerseRef": 139}, {"text": "because mine enemies"}, {"text": "Thy holy words forgotten have,"}, {"text": "and do thy laws despise."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Thy word''s most pure, therefore on it", "bibleVerseRef": 140}, {"text": "thy servant''s love is set."}, {"text": "Small, and despis''d I am, yet I", "bibleVerseRef": 141}, {"text": "thy precepts not forget."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Thy righteousness is righteousness", "bibleVerseRef": 142}, {"text": "which ever doth endure:", "syllables": ["whi-", "ch", "ever", "doth", "en-", "dure:"]}, {"text": "Thy holy law, Lord, also is"}, {"text": "the very truth most pure."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Trouble and anguish have me found,", "syllables": ["trouble", "and", "an-", "gu-", "ish", "have", "me", "found,"], "bibleVerseRef": 143}, {"text": "and taken hold on me:", "syllables": ["and", "take-", "n", "hold", "on", "me:"]}, {"text": "Yet in my trouble my delight"}, {"text": "thy just commandments be."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Eternal righteousness is in", "syllables": ["eter-", "nal", "righ-", "teou-", "s-", "ness", "is", "in"], "bibleVerseRef": 144}, {"text": "thy testimonies all:"}, {"text": "Lord, to me understanding give,"}, {"text": "and ever live I shall.", "syllables": ["and", "ever", "live", "I", "sha-", "ll."]}]}]', 'CM', 'Part 18', 'My zeal hath ev''n consumed me...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (181, 'recy1GmisZnUnthfz', 136, '136 (First Version, Recommended)', '1Give thanks to God, for good is he:
for mercy hath he ever.
2Thanks to the God of gods give ye:
for his grace faileth never.

3Thanks give the Lord of lords unto:
for mercy hath he ever.
4Who only wonders great can do:
for his grace faileth never.

5Who by his wisdom made heav''ns high:
for mercy hath he ever.
6Who stretch''d the earth above the sea:
for his grace faileth never.

7To him that made the great lights shine:
for mercy hath he ever.
8The sun to rule till day decline:
for his grace faileth never.

9The moon and stars to rule by night:
for mercy hath he ever.
10Who Egypt''s first-born kill''d outright:
for his grace faileth never.

11And Isr''el brought from Egypt land:
for mercy hath he ever.
12With stretch''d-out arm, and with strong hand:
for his grace faileth never.

13By whom the Red sea parted was:
for mercy hath he ever.
14And through its midst made Isr''el pass:
for his grace faileth never.

15But Phar''oh and his host did drown:
for mercy hath he ever.
16Who through the desert led his own:
for his grace faileth never.

17To him great kings who overthrew:
for he hath mercy ever.
18Yea, famous kings in battle slew:
for his grace faileth never.

19Ev''n Sihon king of Amorites:
for he hath mercy ever.
20And Og the king of Bashanites:
for his grace faileth never.

21Their land in heritage to have:
(for mercy hath he ever.)
22His servant Isr''el right he gave:
for his grace faileth never.

23In our low state who on us thought:
for he hath mercy ever.
24And from our foes our freedom wrought:
for his grace faileth never.

25Who doth all flesh with food relieve:
for he hath mercy ever.
26Thanks to the God of heaven give:
for his grace faileth never.', NULL, '87 87', 'First Version', 'Give thanks to God, for good is he...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (180, 'recxfSWum4bGVyD0V', 24, '24', '1The earth belongs unto the Lord,
and all that it contains;
The world that is inhabited,
and all that there remains.

2For the foundations thereof
he on the seas did lay,
And he hath it established
upon the floods to stay.

3Who is the man that shall ascend
into the hill of God?
Or who within his holy place
shall have a firm abode?

4Whose hands are clean, whose heart is pure,
and unto vanity
Who hath not lifted up his soul,
nor sworn deceitfully.

5He from th'' Eternal shall receive
the blessing him upon,
And righteousness, ev''n from the God
of his salvation.

6This is the generation
that after him enquire,
O Jacob, who do seek thy face
with their whole heart''s desire.

7Ye gates, lift up your heads on high;
ye doors that last for aye,
Be lifted up, that so the King
of glory enter may.

8But who of glory is the King?
The mighty Lord is this;
Ev''n that same Lord, that great in might
and strong in battle is.

9Ye gates, lift up your heads; ye doors,
doors that do last for aye,
Be lifted up, that so the King
of glory enter may.

10But who is he that is the King
of glory? who is this?
The Lord of hosts, and none but he,
the King of glory is.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "The earth belongs unto the Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "and all that it contains;"}, {"text": "The world that is inhabited,"}, {"text": "and all that there remains."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "For the foundations thereof", "syllables": ["For", "the", "foun-", "da-", "tions", "there-", "-", "of"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "he on the seas did lay,"}, {"text": "And he hath it established"}, {"text": "upon the floods to stay."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Who is the man that shall ascend", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "into the hill of God?"}, {"text": "Or who within his holy place", "syllables": ["Or", "who", "within", "his", "ho-", "ly", "pla-", "ce"]}, {"text": "shall have a firm abode?"}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Whose hands are clean, whose heart is pure,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "and unto vanity"}, {"text": "Who hath not lifted up his soul,"}, {"text": "nor sworn deceitfully."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "He from th'' Eternal shall receive", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "the blessing him upon,"}, {"text": "And righteousness, ev''n from the God"}, {"text": "of his salvation.", "syllables": ["of", "his", "sal-", "va-", "tio-", "n."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "This is the generation", "syllables": ["Thi-", "s", "is", "the", "ge-", "ne-", "ra-", "tion"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "that after him enquire,", "syllables": ["that", "after", "him", "enqu-", "i-", "re,"]}, {"text": "O Jacob, who do seek thy face"}, {"text": "with their whole heart''s desire."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Ye gates, lift up your heads on high;", "syllables": ["Ye", "gates,", "lift", "up", "your", "heads", "on", "high;"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "ye doors that last for aye,"}, {"text": "Be lifted up, that so the King"}, {"text": "of glory enter may."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "But who of glory is the King?", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "The mighty Lord is this;"}, {"text": "Ev''n that same Lord, that great in might"}, {"text": "and strong in battle is."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Ye gates, lift up your heads; ye doors,", "syllables": ["Ye", "gates,", "lift", "up", "your", "heads;", "ye", "doors,"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "doors that do last for aye,"}, {"text": "Be lifted up, that so the King"}, {"text": "of glory enter may."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "But who is he that is the King", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "of glory? who is this?"}, {"text": "The Lord of hosts, and none but he,", "syllables": ["The", "Lord", "of", "hosts,", "and", "none", "but", "he,"]}, {"text": "the King of glory is."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'The earth belongs unto the Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (14, 'rec4rWAW9FS9IjN0a', 150, '150', '1Praise ye the Lord. God''s praise within
his sanctuary raise;
And to him in the firmament
of his pow''r give ye praise.

2Because of all his mighty acts,
with praise him magnify:
O praise him, as he doth excel
in glorious majesty.

3Praise him with trumpet''s sound; his praise
with psaltery advance:
4With timbrel, harp, string''d instruments,
and organs, in the dance.

5Praise him on cymbals loud; him praise
on cymbals sounding high.
6Let each thing breathing praise the Lord.
Praise to the Lord give ye.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Praise ye the Lord. God''s praise within", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "his sanctuary raise;"}, {"text": "And to him in the firmament"}, {"text": "of his pow''r give ye praise."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Because of all his mighty acts,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "with praise him magnify:"}, {"text": "O praise him, as he doth excel"}, {"text": "in glorious majesty."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Praise him with trumpet''s sound; his praise", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "with psaltery advance:", "syllables": ["with", "psalte-", "ry", "ad-", "van-", "ce:"]}, {"text": "With timbrel, harp, string''d instruments,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "and organs, in the dance.", "syllables": ["and", "organs,", "in", "the", "dan-", "ce."]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Praise him on cymbals loud; him praise", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "on cymbals sounding high."}, {"text": "Let each thing breathing praise the Lord.", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "Praise to the Lord give ye."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Praise ye the Lord. God''s praise within...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (1, 'rec085NkMOEgtb5LM', 37, '37', '1For evil-doers fret thou not
thyself unquietly;
Nor do thou envy bear to those
that work iniquity.

2For, even like unto the grass,
soon be cut down shall they;
And, like the green and tender herb,
they wither shall away.

3Set thou thy trust upon the Lord,
and be thou doing good;
And so thou in the land shalt dwell,
and verily have food.

4Delight thyself in God; he''ll give
thine heart''s desire to thee.
5Thy way to God commit, him trust,
it bring to pass shall he.

6And, like unto the light, he shall
thy righteousness display;
And he thy judgment shall bring forth
like noon-tide of the day.

7Rest in the Lord, and patiently
wait for him: do not fref
For him who, prosp''ring in his way,
success in sin doth get.

8Do thou from anger cease, and wrath
see thou forsake also:
Fret not thyself in any wise,
that evil thou should''st do.

9For those that evil doers are
shall be cut off and fall:
But those that wait upon the Lord
the earth inherit shall.

10For yet a little while, and then
the wicked shall not be;
His place thou shalt consider well,
but it thou shalt not see.

11But by inheritance the earth
the meek ones shall possess:
They also shall delight themselves
in an abundant peace.

12The wicked plots against the just,
and at him whets his teeth:
13The Lord shall laugh at him, because
his day he coming seeth.

14The wicked have drawn out the sword,
and bent their bow, to slay
The poor and needy, and to kill
men of an upright way.

15But their own sword, which they have drawn,
shall enter their own heart:
Their bows which they have bent shall break,
and into pieces part.

16A little that a just man hath
is more and better far
Than is the wealth of many such
as lewd and wicked are.

17For sinners'' arms shall broken be;
but God the just sustains.
18God knows the just man''s days, and still
their heritage remains.

19They shall not be asham''d when they
the evil time do see;
And when the days of famine are,
they satisfy''d shall be.

20But wicked men, and foes of God,
as fat of lambs, decay;
They shall consume, yea, into smoke
they shall consume away.

21The wicked borrows, but the same
again he doth not pay;
Whereas the righteous mercy shews,
and gives his own away.

22For such as blessed be of him
the earth inherit shall;
And they that cursed are of him
shall be destroyed all.

23A good man''s footsteps by the Lord
are ordered aright;
And in the way wherein he walks
he greatly doth delight.

24Although he fall, yet shall he not
be cast down utterly;
Because the Lord with his own hand
upholds him mightily.

25I have been young, and now am old,
yet have I never seen
The just man left, nor that his seed
for bread have beggars been.

26He''s ever merciful, and lends:
his seed is bless''d therefore.
27Depart from evil, and do good,
and dwell for evermore.

28For God loves judgment, and his saints
leaves not in any case;
They are kept ever: but cut off
shall be the sinner''s race.

29The just inherit shall the land,
and ever in it dwell:
30The just man''s mouth doth wisdom speak;
his tongue doth judgment tell.

31In''s heart the law is of his God,
his steps slide not away.
32The wicked man doth watch the just,
and seeketh him to slay.

33Yet him the Lord will not forsake,
nor leave him in his hands:
The righteous will he not condemn,
when he in judgment stands.

34Wait on the Lord, and keep his way,
and thee exalt shall he
Th'' earth to inherit; when cut off
the wicked thou shalt see.

35I saw the wicked great in pow''r,
spread like a green bay-tree:
36He pass''d, yea, was not; him I sought,
but found he could not be.

37Mark thou the perfect, and behold
the man of uprightness;
Because that surely of this man
the latter end is peace.

38But those men that transgressors are
shall be destroy''d together;
The latter end of wicked men
shall be cut off for ever.

39But the salvation of the just
is from the Lord above;
He in the time of their distress
their stay and strength doth prove.

40The Lord shall help, and them deliver:
he shall them free and save
From wicked men; because in him
their confidence they have.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "For evil-doers fret thou not", "syllables": ["For", "e-", "vil-", "-doe-", "rs", "fret", "thou", "not"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "thyself unquietly;"}, {"text": "Nor do thou envy bear to those"}, {"text": "that work iniquity."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "For, even like unto the grass,", "syllables": ["For,", "even", "like", "un-", "to", "the", "gra-", "ss,"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "soon be cut down shall they;"}, {"text": "And, like the green and tender herb,"}, {"text": "they wither shall away."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Set thou thy trust upon the Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "and be thou doing good;", "syllables": ["and", "be", "thou", "doi-", "ng", "good;"]}, {"text": "And so thou in the land shalt dwell,"}, {"text": "and verily have food."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Delight thyself in God; he''ll give", "syllables": ["de-", "light", "thyse-", "lf", "in", "God;", "he''ll", "give"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "thine heart''s desire to thee."}, {"text": "Thy way to God commit, him trust,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "it bring to pass shall he."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "And, like unto the light, he shall", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "thy righteousness display;"}, {"text": "And he thy judgment shall bring forth"}, {"text": "like noon-tide of the day.", "syllables": ["like", "noon-ti-", "de", "of", "the", "day."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Rest in the Lord, and patiently", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "wait for him: do not fref"}, {"text": "For him who, prosp''ring in his way,"}, {"text": "success in sin doth get."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Do thou from anger cease, and wrath", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "see thou forsake also:"}, {"text": "Fret not thyself in any wise,", "syllables": ["Fret", "not", "thyse-", "lf", "in", "a-", "ny", "wise,"]}, {"text": "that evil thou should''st do."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "For those that evil doers are", "syllables": ["For", "tho-", "se", "that", "e-", "vil", "doers", "are"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "shall be cut off and fall:"}, {"text": "But those that wait upon the Lord"}, {"text": "the earth inherit shall."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "For yet a little while, and then", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "the wicked shall not be;"}, {"text": "His place thou shalt consider well,"}, {"text": "but it thou shalt not see."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "But by inheritance the earth", "syllables": ["But", "by", "inhe-", "ri-", "tan-", "ce", "the", "earth"], "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "the meek ones shall possess:"}, {"text": "They also shall delight themselves", "syllables": ["They", "also", "shall", "de-", "light", "them-", "sel-", "ves"]}, {"text": "in an abundant peace."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked plots against the just,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "and at him whets his teeth:"}, {"text": "The Lord shall laugh at him, because", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "his day he coming seeth."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked have drawn out the sword,", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "and bent their bow, to slay"}, {"text": "The poor and needy, and to kill"}, {"text": "men of an upright way."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "But their own sword, which they have drawn,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "shall enter their own heart:"}, {"text": "Their bows which they have bent shall break,"}, {"text": "and into pieces part.", "syllables": ["and", "in-", "to", "piece-", "s", "part."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "A little that a just man hath", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "is more and better far"}, {"text": "Than is the wealth of many such"}, {"text": "as lewd and wicked are."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "For sinners'' arms shall broken be;", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "but God the just sustains."}, {"text": "God knows the just man''s days, and still", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "their heritage remains."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "They shall not be asham''d when they", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "the evil time do see;"}, {"text": "And when the days of famine are,"}, {"text": "they satisfy''d shall be."}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "But wicked men, and foes of God,", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "as fat of lambs, decay;"}, {"text": "They shall consume, yea, into smoke", "syllables": ["They", "shall", "consume,", "yea,", "in-", "to", "smo-", "ke"]}, {"text": "they shall consume away."}]}, {"index": 17, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked borrows, but the same", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "again he doth not pay;"}, {"text": "Whereas the righteous mercy shews,", "syllables": ["Wherea-", "s", "the", "righ-", "teous", "mer-", "cy", "shews,"]}, {"text": "and gives his own away."}]}, {"index": 18, "lines": [{"text": "For such as blessed be of him", "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "the earth inherit shall;"}, {"text": "And they that cursed are of him"}, {"text": "shall be destroyed all.", "syllables": ["shall", "be", "des-", "troye-", "d", "all."]}]}, {"index": 19, "lines": [{"text": "A good man''s footsteps by the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 23}, {"text": "are ordered aright;"}, {"text": "And in the way wherein he walks", "syllables": ["And", "in", "the", "way", "wherei-", "n", "he", "walks"]}, {"text": "he greatly doth delight."}]}, {"index": 20, "lines": [{"text": "Although he fall, yet shall he not", "bibleVerseRef": 24}, {"text": "be cast down utterly;"}, {"text": "Because the Lord with his own hand"}, {"text": "upholds him mightily."}]}, {"index": 21, "lines": [{"text": "I have been young, and now am old,", "bibleVerseRef": 25}, {"text": "yet have I never seen"}, {"text": "The just man left, nor that his seed"}, {"text": "for bread have beggars been."}]}, {"index": 22, "lines": [{"text": "He''s ever merciful, and lends:", "syllables": ["He''s", "ever", "mer-", "ci-", "ful,", "and", "le-", "nds:"], "bibleVerseRef": 26}, {"text": "his seed is bless''d therefore."}, {"text": "Depart from evil, and do good,", "bibleVerseRef": 27}, {"text": "and dwell for evermore.", "syllables": ["and", "dwe-", "ll", "for", "ever-", "more."]}]}, {"index": 23, "lines": [{"text": "For God loves judgment, and his saints", "bibleVerseRef": 28}, {"text": "leaves not in any case;"}, {"text": "They are kept ever: but cut off", "syllables": ["They", "are", "kept", "eve-", "r:", "but", "cut", "off"]}, {"text": "shall be the sinner''s race."}]}, {"index": 24, "lines": [{"text": "The just inherit shall the land,", "bibleVerseRef": 29}, {"text": "and ever in it dwell:", "syllables": ["and", "ever", "in", "it", "dwe-", "ll:"]}, {"text": "The just man''s mouth doth wisdom speak;", "bibleVerseRef": 30}, {"text": "his tongue doth judgment tell.", "syllables": ["his", "tongue", "doth", "jud-", "gment", "tell."]}]}, {"index": 25, "lines": [{"text": "In''s heart the law is of his God,", "bibleVerseRef": 31}, {"text": "his steps slide not away.", "syllables": ["his", "steps", "slide", "not", "a-", "way."]}, {"text": "The wicked man doth watch the just,", "bibleVerseRef": 32}, {"text": "and seeketh him to slay."}]}, {"index": 26, "lines": [{"text": "Yet him the Lord will not forsake,", "bibleVerseRef": 33}, {"text": "nor leave him in his hands:"}, {"text": "The righteous will he not condemn,"}, {"text": "when he in judgment stands."}]}, {"index": 27, "lines": [{"text": "Wait on the Lord, and keep his way,", "bibleVerseRef": 34}, {"text": "and thee exalt shall he"}, {"text": "Th'' earth to inherit; when cut off", "syllables": ["Th''", "earth", "to", "inhe-", "rit;", "when", "cut", "off"]}, {"text": "the wicked thou shalt see."}]}, {"index": 28, "lines": [{"text": "I saw the wicked great in pow''r,", "bibleVerseRef": 35}, {"text": "spread like a green bay-tree:"}, {"text": "He pass''d, yea, was not; him I sought,", "bibleVerseRef": 36}, {"text": "but found he could not be."}]}, {"index": 29, "lines": [{"text": "Mark thou the perfect, and behold", "bibleVerseRef": 37}, {"text": "the man of uprightness;"}, {"text": "Because that surely of this man"}, {"text": "the latter end is peace."}]}, {"index": 30, "lines": [{"text": "But those men that transgressors are", "bibleVerseRef": 38}, {"text": "shall be destroy''d together;", "syllables": ["shall", "be", "destroy''d", "to-", "ge-", "ther;"]}, {"text": "The latter end of wicked men"}, {"text": "shall be cut off for ever."}]}, {"index": 31, "lines": [{"text": "But the salvation of the just", "bibleVerseRef": 39}, {"text": "is from the Lord above;"}, {"text": "He in the time of their distress"}, {"text": "their stay and strength doth prove.", "syllables": ["their", "stay", "and", "strength", "doth", "prove."]}]}, {"index": 32, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord shall help, and them deliver:", "bibleVerseRef": 40}, {"text": "he shall them free and save"}, {"text": "From wicked men; because in him"}, {"text": "their confidence they have.", "syllables": ["their", "confi-", "den-", "ce", "they", "have."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'For evil-doers fret thou not...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (2, 'rec0fIvKSY2UrVBfe', 5, '5', '1Give ear unto my words, O Lord,
my meditation weigh.
2Hear my loud cry, my King, my God;
for I to thee will pray.

3Lord, thou shalt early hear my voice:
I early will direct
My pray''r to thee; and, looking up,
an answer will expect.

4For thou art not a God that doth
in wickedness delight;
Neither shall evil dwell with thee,
5Nor fools stand in thy sight.

All that ill-doers are thou hat''st;
6Cutt''st off that liars be:
The bloody and deceitful man
abhorred is by thee.

7But I into thy house will come
in thine abundant grace;
And I will worship in thy fear
toward thy holy place.

8Because of those mine enemies,
Lord, in thy righteousness
Do thou me lead; do thou thy way
make straight before my face.

9For in their mouth there is no truth,
their inward part is ill;
Their throat''s an open sepulchre,
their tongue doth flatter still.

10O God, destroy them; let them be
by their own counsel quell''d:
Them for their many sins cast out,
for they ''gainst thee rebell''d.

11But let all joy that trust in thee,
and still make shouting noise;
For them thou sav''st; let all that love
thy name in thee rejoice.

12For, Lord, unto the righteous man
thou wilt thy blessing yield:
With favour thou wilt compass him
about, as with a shield.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Give ear unto my words, O Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "my meditation weigh."}, {"text": "Hear my loud cry, my King, my God;", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "for I to thee will pray."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, thou shalt early hear my voice:", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "I early will direct", "syllables": ["I", "ear-", "ly", "will", "dire-", "ct"]}, {"text": "My pray''r to thee; and, looking up,"}, {"text": "an answer will expect."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "For thou art not a God that doth", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "in wickedness delight;"}, {"text": "Neither shall evil dwell with thee,"}, {"text": "Nor fools stand in thy sight.", "bibleVerseRef": 5}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "All that ill-doers are thou hat''st;", "syllables": ["All", "that", "il-", "l-doe-", "rs", "are", "thou", "hat''st;"]}, {"text": "Cutt''st off that liars be:", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "The bloody and deceitful man"}, {"text": "abhorred is by thee."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "But I into thy house will come", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "in thine abundant grace;", "syllables": ["in", "thine", "abun-", "dant", "gra-", "ce;"]}, {"text": "And I will worship in thy fear"}, {"text": "toward thy holy place.", "syllables": ["toward", "thy", "ho-", "ly", "pla-", "ce."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Because of those mine enemies,", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "Lord, in thy righteousness"}, {"text": "Do thou me lead; do thou thy way"}, {"text": "make straight before my face."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "For in their mouth there is no truth,", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "their inward part is ill;"}, {"text": "Their throat''s an open sepulchre,"}, {"text": "their tongue doth flatter still.", "syllables": ["their", "tongue", "doth", "flat-", "ter", "still."]}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "O God, destroy them; let them be", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "by their own counsel quell''d:"}, {"text": "Them for their many sins cast out,"}, {"text": "for they ''gainst thee rebell''d."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "But let all joy that trust in thee,", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "and still make shouting noise;"}, {"text": "For them thou sav''st; let all that love"}, {"text": "thy name in thee rejoice."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "For, Lord, unto the righteous man", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "thou wilt thy blessing yield:"}, {"text": "With favour thou wilt compass him"}, {"text": "about, as with a shield."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Give ear unto my words, O Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (56, 'recJZUvym8SF738RN', 66, '66', '1All lands to God in joyful sounds,
aloft your voices raise.
2Sing forth the honour of his name,
and glorious make his praise.

3Say unto God, How terrible
in all thy works art thou!
Through thy great pow''r thy foes to thee
shall be constrain''d to bow.

4All on the earth shall worship thee,
they shall thy praise proclaim
In songs: they shall sing cheerfully
unto thy holy name.

5Come, and the works that God hath wrought
with admiration see:
In''s working to the sons of men
most terrible is he.

6Into dry land the sea he turn''d,
and they a passage had;
Ev''n marching through the flood on foot,
there we in him were glad.

7He ruleth ever by his pow''r;
his eyes the nations see:
O let not the rebellious ones
lift up themselves on high.

8Ye people, bless our God; aloud
the voice speak of his praise:
9Our soul in life who safe preserves,
our foot from sliding stays.

10For thou didst prove and try us, Lord,
as men do silver try;
11Brought''st us into the net,
and mad''st bands on our loins to lie.

12Thou hast caus''d men ride o''er our heads;
and though that we did pass
Through fire and water, yet thou brought''st
us to a wealthy place.

13I''ll bring burnt off ''rings to thy house;
to thee my vows I''ll pay,
14Which my lips utter''d, my mouth spake,
when trouble on me lay.

15Burnt-sacrifices of fat rams
with incense I will bring;
Of bullocks and of goats I will
present an offering.

16All that fear God, come, hear, I''ll tell
what he did for my soul.
17I with my mouth unto him cry''d,
my tongue did him extol.

18If in my heart I sin regard,
the Lord me will not hear:
19But surely God me heard,
and to my prayer''s voice gave ear.

20O let the Lord, our gracious God,
for ever blessed be,
Who turned not my pray''r from him,
nor yet his grace from me.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "All lands to God in joyful sounds,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "aloft your voices raise.", "syllables": ["a-", "loft", "your", "voice-", "s", "raise."]}, {"text": "Sing forth the honour of his name,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "and glorious make his praise."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Say unto God, How terrible", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "in all thy works art thou!"}, {"text": "Through thy great pow''r thy foes to thee"}, {"text": "shall be constrain''d to bow."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "All on the earth shall worship thee,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "they shall thy praise proclaim"}, {"text": "In songs: they shall sing cheerfully"}, {"text": "unto thy holy name."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Come, and the works that God hath wrought", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "with admiration see:"}, {"text": "In''s working to the sons of men"}, {"text": "most terrible is he."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Into dry land the sea he turn''d,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "and they a passage had;"}, {"text": "Ev''n marching through the flood on foot,"}, {"text": "there we in him were glad."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "He ruleth ever by his pow''r;", "syllables": ["He", "rule-", "eth", "ever", "by", "his", "po-", "w''r;"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "his eyes the nations see:"}, {"text": "O let not the rebellious ones"}, {"text": "lift up themselves on high.", "syllables": ["lift", "up", "themsel-", "ves", "on", "high."]}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Ye people, bless our God; aloud", "syllables": ["Ye", "peo-", "ple,", "bless", "our", "God;", "a-", "loud"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "the voice speak of his praise:"}, {"text": "Our soul in life who safe preserves,", "syllables": ["Our", "soul", "in", "life", "who", "safe", "preser-", "ves,"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "our foot from sliding stays."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "For thou didst prove and try us, Lord,", "syllables": ["For", "thou", "didst", "prove", "and", "try", "us,", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "as men do silver try;"}, {"text": "Brought''st us into the net,", "syllables": ["Brou-", "-", "ght''st", "us", "in-", "to", "the", "net,"], "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "and mad''st bands on our loins to lie.", "syllables": ["and", "mad''st", "bands", "on", "our", "loinstolie."]}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Thou hast caus''d men ride o''er our heads;", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "and though that we did pass"}, {"text": "Through fire and water, yet thou brought''st", "syllables": ["Through", "fire", "and", "water,", "yet", "thou", "brou-", "ght''st"]}, {"text": "us to a wealthy place.", "syllables": ["us", "to", "a", "wealthy", "pla-", "ce."]}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "I''ll bring burnt off ''rings to thy house;", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "to thee my vows I''ll pay,"}, {"text": "Which my lips utter''d, my mouth spake,", "syllables": ["Which", "my", "lips", "utter''d,", "my", "mouth", "spa-", "ke,"], "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "when trouble on me lay."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Burnt-sacrifices of fat rams", "syllables": ["bur-", "nt-sa-", "c-", "ri-", "fices", "of", "fat", "rams"], "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "with incense I will bring;", "syllables": ["with", "incen-", "se", "I", "will", "bring;"]}, {"text": "Of bullocks and of goats I will", "syllables": ["Of", "bullocks", "and", "of", "go-", "ats", "I", "will"]}, {"text": "present an offering.", "syllables": ["prese-", "nt", "an", "of-", "fe-", "ring."]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "All that fear God, come, hear, I''ll tell", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "what he did for my soul."}, {"text": "I with my mouth unto him cry''d,", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "my tongue did him extol.", "syllables": ["my", "tongue", "did", "him", "ex-", "tol."]}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "If in my heart I sin regard,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "the Lord me will not hear:"}, {"text": "But surely God me heard,", "syllables": ["But", "sure-", "-", "ly", "God", "me", "hea-", "rd,"], "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "and to my prayer''s voice gave ear.", "syllables": ["and", "to", "my", "prayer''s", "voice", "gaveear."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "O let the Lord, our gracious God,", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "for ever blessed be,", "syllables": ["for", "ever", "ble-", "s-", "sed", "be,"]}, {"text": "Who turned not my pray''r from him,"}, {"text": "nor yet his grace from me.", "syllables": ["nor", "yet", "his", "grace", "from", "me."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'All lands to God in joyful sounds...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (19, 'rec5cTjfRwweevXVI', 119, '119:161-168 (21)', '161Princes have persecuted me,
although no cause they saw:
But still of thy most holy word
my heart doth stand in awe.

162I at thy word rejoice, as one
of spoil that finds great store.
163Thy law I love; but lying all
I hate and do abhor.

164Sev''n times a-day it is my care
to give due praise to thee;
Because of all thy judgments, Lord,
which righteous ever be.

165Great peace have they who love thy law;
offence they shall have none.
166I hop''d for thy salvation, Lord,
and thy commands have done.

167My soul thy testimonies pure
observed carefully;
On them my heart is set, and them
I love exceedingly.

168Thy testimonies and thy laws
I kept with special care;
For all my works and ways each one
before thee open are.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Princes have persecuted me,", "bibleVerseRef": 161}, {"text": "although no cause they saw:"}, {"text": "But still of thy most holy word"}, {"text": "my heart doth stand in awe."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "I at thy word rejoice, as one", "bibleVerseRef": 162}, {"text": "of spoil that finds great store.", "syllables": ["of", "spoil", "that", "finds", "great", "store."]}, {"text": "Thy law I love; but lying all", "syllables": ["Thy", "law", "I", "love-", ";", "but", "lying", "all"], "bibleVerseRef": 163}, {"text": "I hate and do abhor."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Sev''n times a-day it is my care", "bibleVerseRef": 164}, {"text": "to give due praise to thee;"}, {"text": "Because of all thy judgments, Lord,"}, {"text": "which righteous ever be.", "syllables": ["whi-", "ch", "righ-", "teous", "ever", "be."]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Great peace have they who love thy law;", "bibleVerseRef": 165}, {"text": "offence they shall have none.", "syllables": ["offence", "they", "shall", "have", "no-", "ne."]}, {"text": "I hop''d for thy salvation, Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 166}, {"text": "and thy commands have done."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "My soul thy testimonies pure", "bibleVerseRef": 167}, {"text": "observed carefully;"}, {"text": "On them my heart is set, and them"}, {"text": "I love exceedingly."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Thy testimonies and thy laws", "bibleVerseRef": 168}, {"text": "I kept with special care;", "syllables": ["I", "kept", "with", "speci-", "al", "care;"]}, {"text": "For all my works and ways each one"}, {"text": "before thee open are.", "syllables": ["be-", "fo-", "re", "thee", "open", "are."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Princes have persecuted me...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (25, 'rec6plJYPGFMeBuzw', 100, '100 (First Version, Recommended)', '1All people that on earth do dwell,
Sing to the Lord with cheerful voice.
2Him serve with mirth, his praise forth tell,
Come ye before him and rejoice.

3Know that the Lord is God indeed;
Without our aid he did us make:
We are his flock, he doth us feed,
And for his sheep he doth us take.

4O enter then his gates with praise,
Approach with joy his courts unto:
Praise, laud, and bless his name always,
For it is seemly so to do.

5For why? the Lord our God is good,
His mercy is for ever sure;
His truth at all times firmly stood,
And shall from age to age endure.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "All people that on earth do dwell,", "syllables": ["All", "peo-", "ple", "that", "on", "earth", "do", "dwell,"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "Sing to the Lord with cheerful voice."}, {"text": "Him serve with mirth, his praise forth tell,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "Come ye before him and rejoice."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Know that the Lord is God indeed;", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "Without our aid he did us make:"}, {"text": "We are his flock, he doth us feed,"}, {"text": "And for his sheep he doth us take."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "O enter then his gates with praise,", "syllables": ["O", "enter", "then", "his", "ga-", "tes", "with", "praise,"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "Approach with joy his courts unto:", "syllables": ["appro-", "ach", "with", "joy", "his", "courts", "un-", "to:"]}, {"text": "Praise, laud, and bless his name always,"}, {"text": "For it is seemly so to do."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "For why? the Lord our God is good,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "His mercy is for ever sure;", "syllables": ["His", "mer-", "cy", "is", "for", "ever", "sure-", ";"]}, {"text": "His truth at all times firmly stood,"}, {"text": "And shall from age to age endure."}]}]', 'LM (long meter, 88 88)', 'First Version', 'All people that on earth do dwell...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (26, 'rec75zBXUeDZ78a9b', 119, '119:17-24 (3)', '17With me thy servant, in thy grace,
deal bountifully, Lord:
That by thy favor I may live,
and duly keep thy word.

18Open mine eyes, that of thy law
the wonders I may see.
19I am a stranger on this earth,
hide not thy laws from me.

20My soul within me breaks,
and doth much fainting still endure,
Through longing that it hath all times
unto thy judgments pure.

21Thou hast rebuk''d the cursed proud,
who from thy precepts swerve.
22Reproach and shame remove from me,
for I thy laws observe.

23Against me princes spake with spite,
while they in council sat:
But I thy servant did upon
thy statutes meditate.

24My comfort, and my heart''s delight,
thy testimonies be;
And they, in all my doubts and fears,
are counsellors to me.
', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "With me thy servant, in thy grace,", "syllables": ["With", "me", "thy", "servant,", "in", "thy", "gra-", "ce,"], "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "deal bountifully, Lord:"}, {"text": "That by thy favor I may live,"}, {"text": "and duly keep thy word."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Open mine eyes, that of thy law", "syllables": ["Open", "mine", "eye-", "s,", "that", "of", "thy", "law"], "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "the wonders I may see."}, {"text": "I am a stranger on this earth,", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "hide not thy laws from me."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "My soul within me breaks,", "syllables": ["My", "soul", "wi-", "thin", "me", "brea-", "-", "ks,"], "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "and doth much fainting still endure,", "syllables": ["and", "doth", "much", "fainting", "still", "endure,"]}, {"text": "Through longing that it hath all times"}, {"text": "unto thy judgments pure."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Thou hast rebuk''d the cursed proud,", "bibleVerseRef": 21}, {"text": "who from thy precepts swerve."}, {"text": "Reproach and shame remove from me,", "syllables": ["repro-", "ach", "and", "shame", "re-", "move", "from", "me,"], "bibleVerseRef": 22}, {"text": "for I thy laws observe.", "syllables": ["for", "I", "thy", "laws", "obser-", "ve."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Against me princes spake with spite,", "syllables": ["against", "me", "princes", "spa-", "ke", "with", "spi-", "te,"], "bibleVerseRef": 23}, {"text": "while they in council sat:"}, {"text": "But I thy servant did upon"}, {"text": "thy statutes meditate.", "syllables": ["thy", "statu-", "tes", "me-", "di-", "tate."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "My comfort, and my heart''s delight,", "bibleVerseRef": 24}, {"text": "thy testimonies be;"}, {"text": "And they, in all my doubts and fears,"}, {"text": "are counsellors to me."}]}]', 'CM', 'Part 3', 'With me thy servant, in thy grace...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (35, 'rec9UrZK30zo0YBLv', 23, '23', '1The Lord''s my shepherd, I''ll not want.
2He makes me down to lie
In pastures green: he leadeth me
the quiet waters by.

3My soul he doth restore again;
and me to walk doth make
Within the paths of righteousness,
ev''n for his own name''s sake.

4Yea, though I walk in death''s dark vale,
yet will I fear none ill:
For thou art with me; and thy rod
and staff me comfort still.

5My table thou hast furnished
in presence of my foes;
My head thou dost with oil anoint,
and my cup overflows.

6Goodness and mercy all my life
shall surely follow me:
And in God''s house for evermore
my dwelling-place shall be.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord''s my shepherd, I''ll not want.", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "He makes me down to lie", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "In pastures green: he leadeth me"}, {"text": "the quiet waters by."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "My soul he doth restore again;", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "and me to walk doth make"}, {"text": "Within the paths of righteousness,"}, {"text": "ev''n for his own name''s sake."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Yea, though I walk in death''s dark vale,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "yet will I fear none ill:", "syllables": ["yet", "will", "I", "fear", "none", "ill:"]}, {"text": "For thou art with me; and thy rod"}, {"text": "and staff me comfort still."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "My table thou hast furnished", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "in presence of my foes;"}, {"text": "My head thou dost with oil anoint,"}, {"text": "and my cup overflows.", "syllables": ["and", "my", "cup", "over-", "flo-", "ws."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Goodness and mercy all my life", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "shall surely follow me:"}, {"text": "And in God''s house for evermore", "syllables": ["And", "in", "Go-", "d''s", "house", "for", "ever-", "more"]}, {"text": "my dwelling-place shall be.", "syllables": ["my", "dwellin-", "g-pla-", "ce", "shall", "be."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'The Lord''s my shepherd, I''ll not want...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (29, 'rec7l97PzRFDht8Rk', 45, '45 (First Version)', '1My heart brings forth a goodly thing;
my words that I indite
Concern the King: my tongue''s a pen
of one that swift doth write.

2Thou fairer art than sons of men:
into thy lips is store
Of grace infus''d; God therefore thee
hath bless''d for evermore.

3O thou that art the mighty One,
thy sword gird on thy thigh;
Ev''n with thy glory excellent,
and with thy majesty.

4For meekness, truth, and righteousness,
in state ride prosp''rously;
And thy right hand shall thee instruct
in things that fearful be.

5Thine arrows sharply pierce the heart
of th'' en''mies of the King;
And under thy subjection
the people down do bring.

6For ever and for ever is,
O God, thy throne of might;
The sceptre of thy kingdom is
a sceptre that is right.

7Thou lovest right, and hatest ill;
for God, thy God, most high,
Above thy fellows hath with th'' oil
of joy anointed thee.

8Of aloes, myrrh,
and cassia, a smell thy garments had,
Out of the iv''ry palaces,
whereby they made thee glad.

9Among thy women honourable
kings'' daughters were at hand:
Upon thy right hand did the queen
in gold of Ophir stand.

10O daughter, hearken and regard,
and do thine ear incline;
Likewise forget thy father''s house,
and people that are thine.

11Then of the King desir''d shall be
thy beauty veh''mently:
Because he is thy Lord, do thou
him worship rev''rently.

12The daughter there of Tyre shall be
with gifts and off ''rings great:
Those of the people that are rich
thy favour shall entreat.

13Behold, the daughter of the King
all glorious is within;
And with embroideries of gold
her garments wrought have been.

14She shall be brought unto the King
in robes with needle wrought;
Her fellow-virgins following
shall unto thee be brought.

15They shall be brought with gladness great,
and mirth on ev''ry side,
Into the palace of the King,
and there they shall abide.

16Instead of those thy fathers dear,
thy children thou may''st take,
And in all places of the earth
them noble princes make.

17Thy name remember''d I will make
through ages all to be:
The people therefore evermore
shall praises give to thee.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "My heart brings forth a goodly thing;", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "my words that I indite"}, {"text": "Concern the King: my tongue''s a pen", "syllables": ["concern", "the", "King:", "my", "ton-", "gue''s", "a", "pen"]}, {"text": "of one that swift doth write.", "syllables": ["of", "one", "that", "swift", "doth", "write."]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Thou fairer art than sons of men:", "syllables": ["Thou", "faire-", "r", "art", "than", "sons", "of", "men:"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "into thy lips is store", "syllables": ["into", "thy", "lips", "is", "sto-", "re"]}, {"text": "Of grace infus''d; God therefore thee", "syllables": ["Of", "grace", "in-", "fus''d;", "God", "there-", "fore", "thee"]}, {"text": "hath bless''d for evermore.", "syllables": ["hath", "ble-", "ss''d", "for", "ever-", "more."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "O thou that art the mighty One,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "thy sword gird on thy thigh;"}, {"text": "Ev''n with thy glory excellent,", "syllables": ["Ev''n", "with", "thy", "glo-", "ry", "ex-", "celle-", "nt,"]}, {"text": "and with thy majesty."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "For meekness, truth, and righteousness,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "in state ride prosp''rously;"}, {"text": "And thy right hand shall thee instruct"}, {"text": "in things that fearful be."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Thine arrows sharply pierce the heart", "syllables": ["Thine", "arrows", "shar-", "ply", "pier-", "ce", "the", "heart"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "of th'' en''mies of the King;", "syllables": ["of", "th''", "en''mies", "of", "the", "King;"]}, {"text": "And under thy subjection", "syllables": ["And", "un-", "der", "thy", "su-", "b-", "jec-", "tion"]}, {"text": "the people down do bring.", "syllables": ["the", "peo-", "ple", "down", "do", "bring."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "For ever and for ever is,", "syllables": ["For", "eve-", "-", "r", "and", "for", "ever", "is,"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "O God, thy throne of might;", "syllables": ["O", "God,", "thy", "throne", "of", "might;"]}, {"text": "The sceptre of thy kingdom is", "syllables": ["The", "sce-", "ptre", "of", "thy", "kin-", "gdom", "is"]}, {"text": "a sceptre that is right.", "syllables": ["a", "sce-", "ptre", "that", "is", "right."]}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "Thou lovest right, and hatest ill;", "syllables": ["Thou", "love-", "st", "ri-", "ght,", "and", "hatest", "ill;"], "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "for God, thy God, most high,"}, {"text": "Above thy fellows hath with th'' oil", "syllables": ["above", "thy", "fel-", "lows", "hath", "with", "th''", "oil"]}, {"text": "of joy anointed thee."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "Of aloes, myrrh,", "syllables": ["Of", "a-", "loe-", "-", "-", "s,", "my-", "rrh,"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "and cassia, a smell thy garments had,", "syllables": ["and", "cassia,", "a", "smell", "thy", "garmentshad,"]}, {"text": "Out of the iv''ry palaces,", "syllables": ["Out", "of", "the", "iv-", "''ry", "pa-", "lace-", "s,"]}, {"text": "whereby they made thee glad."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Among thy women honourable", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "kings'' daughters were at hand:"}, {"text": "Upon thy right hand did the queen"}, {"text": "in gold of Ophir stand."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "O daughter, hearken and regard,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "and do thine ear incline;", "syllables": ["and", "do", "thine", "ear", "incli-", "ne;"]}, {"text": "Likewise forget thy father''s house,"}, {"text": "and people that are thine.", "syllables": ["and", "peo-", "ple", "that", "are", "thine."]}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Then of the King desir''d shall be", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "thy beauty veh''mently:"}, {"text": "Because he is thy Lord, do thou"}, {"text": "him worship rev''rently."}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "The daughter there of Tyre shall be", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "with gifts and off ''rings great:"}, {"text": "Those of the people that are rich", "syllables": ["Those", "of", "the", "peo-", "ple", "that", "are", "rich"]}, {"text": "thy favour shall entreat."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "Behold, the daughter of the King", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "all glorious is within;"}, {"text": "And with embroideries of gold"}, {"text": "her garments wrought have been."}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "She shall be brought unto the King", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "in robes with needle wrought;", "syllables": ["in", "robes", "with", "needle", "wrou-", "ght;"]}, {"text": "Her fellow-virgins following"}, {"text": "shall unto thee be brought."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "They shall be brought with gladness great,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "and mirth on ev''ry side,"}, {"text": "Into the palace of the King,"}, {"text": "and there they shall abide."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "Instead of those thy fathers dear,", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "thy children thou may''st take,"}, {"text": "And in all places of the earth"}, {"text": "them noble princes make."}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "Thy name remember''d I will make", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "through ages all to be:", "syllables": ["throu-", "gh", "ages", "all", "to", "be:"]}, {"text": "The people therefore evermore"}, {"text": "shall praises give to thee.", "syllables": ["shall", "praise-", "s", "give", "to", "thee."]}]}]', 'CM', 'First Version', 'My heart brings forth a goodly thing...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (36, 'rec9XY8DiWRc7HwMn', 113, '113', '1Praise God: ye servants of the Lord,
O praise, the Lord''s name praise.
2Yea, blessed be the name of God
from this time forth always.

3From rising sun to where it sets,
God''s name is to be prais''d.
4Above all nations God is high,
''bove heav''ns his glory rais''d.

5Unto the Lord our God that dwells
on high, who can compare?
6Himself that humbleth things to see
in heav''n and earth that are.

7He from the dust doth raise the poor,
that very low doth lie;
And from the dunghill lifts the man
oppress''d with poverty;

8That he may highly him advance,
and with the princes set;
With those that of his people are
the chief, ev''n princes great.

9The barren woman house to keep
he maketh, and to be
Of sons a mother full of joy.
Praise to the Lord give ye.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Praise God: ye servants of the Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "O praise, the Lord''s name praise."}, {"text": "Yea, blessed be the name of God", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "from this time forth always."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "From rising sun to where it sets,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "God''s name is to be prais''d."}, {"text": "Above all nations God is high,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "''bove heav''ns his glory rais''d.", "syllables": ["''bove", "heav''ns", "his", "glo-", "ry", "rais''d."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Unto the Lord our God that dwells", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "on high, who can compare?"}, {"text": "Himself that humbleth things to see", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "in heav''n and earth that are."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "He from the dust doth raise the poor,", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "that very low doth lie;"}, {"text": "And from the dunghill lifts the man"}, {"text": "oppress''d with poverty;", "syllables": ["op-", "pre-", "ss''d", "with", "pover-", "ty;"]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "That he may highly him advance,", "syllables": ["That", "he", "may", "highly", "him", "ad-", "van-", "ce,"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "and with the princes set;"}, {"text": "With those that of his people are", "syllables": ["With", "those", "that", "of", "his", "peo-", "ple", "are"]}, {"text": "the chief, ev''n princes great."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "The barren woman house to keep", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "he maketh, and to be"}, {"text": "Of sons a mother full of joy."}, {"text": "Praise to the Lord give ye."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Praise God: ye servants of the Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (42, 'recD49DwrsHHHwwMX', 9, '9', '1Lord, thee I''ll praise with all my heart,
thy wonders all proclaim.
2In thee, most High, I''ll greatly joy,
and sing unto thy name.

3When back my foes were turn''d, they fell,
and perish''d at thy sight:
4For thou maintain''dst my right and cause;
on throne sat''st judging right.

5The heathen thou rebuked hast,
the wicked overthrown;
Thou hast put out their names, that they
may never more be known.

6O en''my! now destructions have
an end perpetual:
Thou cities raz''d; perish''d with them
is their memorial.

7God shall endure for aye; he doth
for judgment set his throne;
8In righteousness to judge the world,
justice to give each one.

9God also will a refuge be
for those that are oppress''d;
A refuge will he be in times
of trouble to distress''d.

10And they that know thy name, in thee
their confidence will place:
For thou hast not forsaken them
that truly seek thy face.

11O sing ye praises to the Lord,
that dwells in Sion hill;
And all the nations among
his deeds record ye still.

12When he enquireth after blood,
he then rememb''reth them:
The humble folk he not forgets
that call upon his name.

13Lord, pity me; behold the grief
which I from foes sustain;
Ev''n thou, who from the gates of death
dost raise me up again;

14That I, in Sion''s daughters'' gates,
may all thy praise advance;
And that I may rejoice always
in thy deliverance.

15The heathen are sunk in the pit
which they themselves prepar''d;
And in the net which they have hid
their own feet fast are snar''d.

16The Lord is by the judgment known
which he himself hath wrought:
The sinners'' hands do make the snares
wherewith themselves are caught.

17They who are wicked into hell
each one shall turned be;
And all the nations that forget
to seek the Lord most high.

18For they that needy are shall not
forgotten be alway;
The expectation of the poor
shall not be lost for aye.

19Arise, Lord, let not man prevail;
judge heathen in thy sight:
20That they may know themselves but men,
the nations, Lord, affright.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, thee I''ll praise with all my heart,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "thy wonders all proclaim."}, {"text": "In thee, most High, I''ll greatly joy,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "and sing unto thy name."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "When back my foes were turn''d, they fell,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "and perish''d at thy sight:"}, {"text": "For thou maintain''dst my right and cause;", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "on throne sat''st judging right.", "syllables": ["on", "throne", "sat''st", "jud-", "ging", "right."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "The heathen thou rebuked hast,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "the wicked overthrown;", "syllables": ["the", "wic-", "ked", "over-", "thro-", "wn;"]}, {"text": "Thou hast put out their names, that they"}, {"text": "may never more be known."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "O en''my! now destructions have", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "an end perpetual:"}, {"text": "Thou cities raz''d; perish''d with them"}, {"text": "is their memorial."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "God shall endure for aye; he doth", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "for judgment set his throne;", "syllables": ["for", "judgment", "set", "his", "thro-", "ne;"]}, {"text": "In righteousness to judge the world,", "syllables": ["In", "righteous-", "ness", "to", "jud-", "ge", "the", "world,"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "justice to give each one."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "God also will a refuge be", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "for those that are oppress''d;"}, {"text": "A refuge will he be in times"}, {"text": "of trouble to distress''d."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "And they that know thy name, in thee", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "their confidence will place:", "syllables": ["their", "confiden-", "ce", "will", "pla-", "ce:"]}, {"text": "For thou hast not forsaken them", "syllables": ["For", "thou", "hast", "not", "for-", "sake-", "n", "them"]}, {"text": "that truly seek thy face."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "O sing ye praises to the Lord,", "syllables": ["O", "sing", "ye", "praise-", "s", "to", "the", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "that dwells in Sion hill;", "syllables": ["that", "dwe-", "lls", "in", "Sion", "hill;"]}, {"text": "And all the nations among", "syllables": ["And", "all", "the", "na-", "tio-", "ns", "a-", "mong"]}, {"text": "his deeds record ye still."}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "When he enquireth after blood,", "syllables": ["When", "he", "enqu-", "i-", "reth", "af-", "ter", "blood,"], "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "he then rememb''reth them:"}, {"text": "The humble folk he not forgets"}, {"text": "that call upon his name."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, pity me; behold the grief", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "which I from foes sustain;"}, {"text": "Ev''n thou, who from the gates of death", "syllables": ["Ev''n", "thou,", "who", "from", "the", "gates", "of", "death"]}, {"text": "dost raise me up again;"}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "That I, in Sion''s daughters'' gates,", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "may all thy praise advance;", "syllables": ["may", "all", "thy", "praise", "advan-", "ce;"]}, {"text": "And that I may rejoice always"}, {"text": "in thy deliverance.", "syllables": ["in", "thy", "deli-", "ve-", "ran-", "ce."]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "The heathen are sunk in the pit", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "which they themselves prepar''d;", "syllables": ["which", "they", "themsel-", "ves", "pre-", "par''d;"]}, {"text": "And in the net which they have hid"}, {"text": "their own feet fast are snar''d."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord is by the judgment known", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "which he himself hath wrought:"}, {"text": "The sinners'' hands do make the snares", "syllables": ["The", "sinners''", "hands", "do", "make", "the", "sna-", "res"]}, {"text": "wherewith themselves are caught.", "syllables": ["wherewith", "them-", "sel-", "ves", "are", "caught."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "They who are wicked into hell", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "each one shall turned be;"}, {"text": "And all the nations that forget"}, {"text": "to seek the Lord most high."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "For they that needy are shall not", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "forgotten be alway;"}, {"text": "The expectation of the poor"}, {"text": "shall not be lost for aye."}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "Arise, Lord, let not man prevail;", "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "judge heathen in thy sight:", "syllables": ["judge", "hea-", "then", "in", "thy", "sight:"]}, {"text": "That they may know themselves but men,", "syllables": ["That", "they", "may", "know", "themsel-", "ves", "but", "men,"], "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "the nations, Lord, affright."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Lord, thee I''ll praise with all my heart...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (43, 'recDn6Yr3LtrKsaFB', 94, '94', '1O Lord God, unto whom alone
all vengeance doth belong;
O mighty God, who vengeance own''st,
shine forth, avenging wrong.

2Lift up thyself, thou of the earth
the sov''reign Judge that art;
And unto those that are so proud
a due reward impart.

3How long, O mighty God, shall they
who lewd and wicked be,
How long shall they who wicked are
thus triumph haughtily?

4How long shall things most hard by them
be uttered and told?
And all that work iniquity
to boast themselves be bold?

5Thy folk they break in pieces, Lord,
thine heritage oppress:
6The widow they and stranger slay,
and kill the fatherless.

7Yet say they, God it shall not see,
nor God of Jacob know.
8Ye brutish people! understand;
fools! when wise will ye grow?

9The Lord did plant the ear of man,
and hear then shall not he?
He only form''d the eye, and
then shall he not clearly see?

10He that the nations doth correct,
shall he not chastise you?
He knowledge unto man doth teach,
and shall himself not know?

11Man''s thoughts to be but vanity
the Lord doth well discern.
12Bless''d is the man thou chast''nest, Lord,
and mak''st thy law to learn:

13That thou may''st give him rest from days
of sad adversity,
Until the pit be digg''d for those
that work iniquity.

14For sure the Lord will not cast off
those that his people be,
Neither his own inheritance
quit and forsake will he:

15But judgment unto righteousness
shall yet return again;
And all shall follow after it
that are right-hearted men.

16Who will rise up for me against
those that do wickedly?
Who will stand up for me ''gainst those
that work iniquity?

17Unless the Lord had been my help
when I was sore opprest,
Almost my soul had in the house
of silence been at rest.

18When I had uttered this word,
(my foot doth slip away,)
Thy mercy held me up, O Lord,
thy goodness did me stay.

19Amidst the multitude of thoughts
which in my heart do fight,
My soul, lest it be overcharg''d,
thy comforts do delight.

20Shall of iniquity the throne
have fellowship with thee,
Which mischief, cunningly contriv''d,
doth by a law decree?

21Against the righteous souls they join,
they guiltless blood condemn.
22But of my refuge God''s the rock,
and my defence from them.

23On them their own iniquity
the Lord shall bring and lay,
And cut them off in their own sin;
our Lord God shall them slay.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord God, unto whom alone", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "all vengeance doth belong;", "syllables": ["all", "vengean-", "ce", "doth", "be-", "long;"]}, {"text": "O mighty God, who vengeance own''st,", "syllables": ["O", "mighty", "God,", "who", "ven-", "gean-", "ce", "own''st,"]}, {"text": "shine forth, avenging wrong.", "syllables": ["shine", "fo-", "rth,", "aven-", "ging", "wrong."]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Lift up thyself, thou of the earth", "syllables": ["Lift", "up", "thyse-", "lf,", "thou", "of", "the", "earth"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "the sov''reign Judge that art;", "syllables": ["the", "sov''reign", "jud-", "ge", "that", "art;"]}, {"text": "And unto those that are so proud"}, {"text": "a due reward impart."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "How long, O mighty God, shall they", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "who lewd and wicked be,"}, {"text": "How long shall they who wicked are"}, {"text": "thus triumph haughtily?", "syllables": ["thus", "triu-", "mph", "haug-", "hti-", "ly?"]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "How long shall things most hard by them", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "be uttered and told?"}, {"text": "And all that work iniquity"}, {"text": "to boast themselves be bold?", "syllables": ["to", "boast", "themsel-", "ves", "be", "bold?"]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "Thy folk they break in pieces, Lord,", "syllables": ["Thy", "folk", "they", "break", "in", "piece-", "s,", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "thine heritage oppress:"}, {"text": "The widow they and stranger slay,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "and kill the fatherless."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Yet say they, God it shall not see,", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "nor God of Jacob know."}, {"text": "Ye brutish people! understand;", "syllables": ["Ye", "brutish", "pe-", "o-", "ple!", "un-", "der-", "stand;"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "fools! when wise will ye grow?"}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord did plant the ear of man,", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "and hear then shall not he?"}, {"text": "He only form''d the eye, and", "syllables": ["He", "on-", "ly", "fo-", "rm''d", "the", "eye,", "and"]}, {"text": "then shall he not clearly see?", "syllables": ["then", "shall", "he", "not", "clearly", "see?"]}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "He that the nations doth correct,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "shall he not chastise you?"}, {"text": "He knowledge unto man doth teach,", "syllables": ["He", "knowled-", "ge", "un-", "to", "man", "doth", "teach,"]}, {"text": "and shall himself not know?"}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "Man''s thoughts to be but vanity", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "the Lord doth well discern."}, {"text": "Bless''d is the man thou chast''nest, Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "and mak''st thy law to learn:"}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "That thou may''st give him rest from days", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "of sad adversity,"}, {"text": "Until the pit be digg''d for those"}, {"text": "that work iniquity."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "For sure the Lord will not cast off", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "those that his people be,", "syllables": ["those", "that", "his", "peo-", "ple", "be,"]}, {"text": "Neither his own inheritance", "syllables": ["neither", "his", "own", "i-", "nhe-", "ri-", "tan-", "ce"]}, {"text": "quit and forsake will he:", "syllables": ["quit", "and", "for-", "sake", "will", "he:"]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "But judgment unto righteousness", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "shall yet return again;"}, {"text": "And all shall follow after it"}, {"text": "that are right-hearted men."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "Who will rise up for me against", "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "those that do wickedly?"}, {"text": "Who will stand up for me ''gainst those"}, {"text": "that work iniquity?"}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text"