in songs their voices raise:

Thou''lt justly people judge,
on earth rule nations all.
5Let people praise thee, Lord; let them
praise thee, both great and small.

6The earth her fruit shall yield,
our God shall blessing send.
7God shall us bless; men shall him fear
unto earth''s utmost end.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, bless and pity us,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "shine on us with thy face:"}, {"text": "That th'' earth thy way, and nations all", "syllables": ["That", "th''", "earth", "thy", "way,", "and", "nations", "all"], "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "may know thy saving grace.", "syllables": ["may", "know", "thy", "saving", "gra-", "ce."]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Let people praise thee, Lord;", "syllables": ["Let", "peo-", "ple", "praise", "thee,", "Lord;"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "let people all thee praise.", "syllables": ["let", "peo-", "ple", "all", "thee", "praise."]}, {"text": "O let the nations be glad,", "syllables": ["O", "let", "the", "na-", "tio-", "ns", "be", "glad,"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "in songs their voices raise:", "syllables": ["in", "songs", "their", "voice-", "s", "raise:"]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Thou''lt justly people judge,", "syllables": ["Thou''lt", "justly", "peo-", "ple", "jud-", "ge,"]}, {"text": "on earth rule nations all."}, {"text": "Let people praise thee, Lord; let them", "syllables": ["Let", "peo-", "ple", "praise", "thee,", "Lord;", "let", "them"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "praise thee, both great and small."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "The earth her fruit shall yield,", "syllables": ["The", "earth", "her", "fruit", "shall", "yield,"], "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "our God shall blessing send."}, {"text": "God shall us bless; men shall him fear", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "unto earth''s utmost end."}]}]', 'SM', 'First Version', 'Lord, bless and pity us...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (105, 'recc6MeMdOT6M0KdY', 70, '70 (Second Version)', '1Make haste, O God, me to preserve;
with speed, Lord, succour me
2Let them that for my soul do seek
sham''d and confounded be:

Let them be turned back, and sham''d,
that in my hurt delight
3Turn''d back be they, Ha, ha! that say,
their shaming to requite.

4O Lord, in thee let all be glad,
and joy that seek for thee:
Let them who thy salvation love
say still, God praised be.

5But I both poor and needy am;
come, Lord, and make no stay:
My help thou and deliv''rer art;
O Lord, make no delay.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Make haste, O God, me to preserve;", "syllables": ["Make", "haste,", "O", "God,", "me", "to", "pre-", "serve;"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "with speed, Lord, succour me"}, {"text": "Let them that for my soul do seek", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "sham''d and confounded be:"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Let them be turned back, and sham''d,"}, {"text": "that in my hurt delight"}, {"text": "Turn''d back be they, Ha, ha! that say,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "their shaming to requite.", "syllables": ["their", "shaming", "to", "requ-", "i-", "te."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord, in thee let all be glad,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "and joy that seek for thee:"}, {"text": "Let them who thy salvation love"}, {"text": "say still, God praised be.", "syllables": ["say", "still,", "God", "praise-", "d", "be."]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "But I both poor and needy am;", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "come, Lord, and make no stay:"}, {"text": "My help thou and deliv''rer art;"}, {"text": "O Lord, make no delay."}]}]', 'CM', 'Second Version', 'Make haste, O God, me to preserve...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (113, 'receUWysUTrwJJXLw', 15, '15', '1Within thy tabernacle, Lord,
who shall abide with thee?
And in thy high and holy hill
who shall a dweller be?

2The man that walketh uprightly,
and worketh righteousness,
And as he thinketh in his heart,
so doth he truth express.

3Who doth not slander with his tongue,
nor to his friend doth hurt;
Nor yet against his neighbour doth
take up an ill report.

4In whose eyes vile men are despis''d;
but those that God do fear
He honoureth; and changeth not,
though to his hurt he swear.

5His coin puts not to usury,
nor take reward will he
Against the guiltless. Who doth
thus shall never moved be.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Within thy tabernacle, Lord,", "syllables": ["wi-", "thin", "thy", "tabe-", "r-", "nac-", "le,", "Lord,"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "who shall abide with thee?"}, {"text": "And in thy high and holy hill"}, {"text": "who shall a dweller be?"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The man that walketh uprightly,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "and worketh righteousness,"}, {"text": "And as he thinketh in his heart,"}, {"text": "so doth he truth express."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Who doth not slander with his tongue,", "syllables": ["Who", "doth", "not", "slander", "with", "his", "ton-", "gue,"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "nor to his friend doth hurt;"}, {"text": "Nor yet against his neighbour doth"}, {"text": "take up an ill report."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "In whose eyes vile men are despis''d;", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "but those that God do fear"}, {"text": "He honoureth; and changeth not,"}, {"text": "though to his hurt he swear."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "His coin puts not to usury,", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "nor take reward will he"}, {"text": "Against the guiltless. Who doth"}, {"text": "thus shall never moved be.", "syllables": ["thus", "shall", "never", "mo-", "ved", "be."]}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Within thy tabernacle, Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (68, 'recPhdYMedyV5U2mW', 127, '127', '1Except the Lord do build the house,
the builders lose their pain:
Except the Lord the city keep,
the watchmen watch in vain.

2''Tis vain for you to rise betimes,
or late from rest to keep,
To feed on sorrows'' bread;
so gives he his beloved sleep.

3Lo, children are God''s heritage,
the womb''s fruit his reward.
4The sons of youth as arrows are,
for strong men''s hands prepar''d.

5O happy is the man that hath
his quiver fill''d with those;
They unashamed in the gate
shall speak unto their foes.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Except the Lord do build the house,", "syllables": ["except", "the", "Lord", "do", "bu-", "ild", "the", "house,"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "the builders lose their pain:", "syllables": ["the", "bui-", "lders", "lose", "their", "pain:"]}, {"text": "Except the Lord the city keep,"}, {"text": "the watchmen watch in vain."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "''Tis vain for you to rise betimes,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "or late from rest to keep,"}, {"text": "To feed on sorrows'' bread;", "syllables": ["To", "feed", "on", "sor-", "ro-", "ws''", "brea-", "d;"]}, {"text": "so gives he his beloved sleep.", "syllables": ["so", "gives", "he", "his", "beloved", "sleep."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Lo, children are God''s heritage,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "the womb''s fruit his reward.", "syllables": ["the", "womb''s", "fruit", "his", "re-", "ward."]}, {"text": "The sons of youth as arrows are,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "for strong men''s hands prepar''d."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "O happy is the man that hath", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "his quiver fill''d with those;", "syllables": ["his", "qui-", "ver", "fill''d", "with", "those;"]}, {"text": "They unashamed in the gate"}, {"text": "shall speak unto their foes."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Except the Lord do build the house...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (119, 'recgZOYPOZp2VhLez', 10, '10', '1Wherefore is it that thou, O Lord,
dost stand from us afar?
And wherefore hidest thou thyself,
when times so troublous are?

2The wicked in his loftiness
doth persecute the poor:
In these devices they have fram''d
let them be taken sure.

3The wicked of his heart''s desire
doth talk with boasting great;
He blesseth him that''s covetous,
whom yet the Lord doth hate.

4The wicked, through his pride of face,
on God he doth not call;
And in the counsels of his heart
the Lord is not at all.

5His ways they always grievous are;
thy judgments from his sight
Removed are: at all his foes
he puffeth with despight.

6Within his heart he thus hath said,
I shall not moved be;
And no adversity at all
shall ever come to me.

7His mouth with cursing, fraud, deceit,
is fill''d abundantly;
And underneath his tongue there is
mischief and vanity.

8He closely sits in villages;
he slays the innocent:
Against the poor that pass him by
his cruel eyes are bent.

9He, lion-like, lurks in his den;
he waits the poor to take;
And when he draws him in his net,
his prey he doth him make.

10Himself he humbleth very low,
he croucheth down withal,
That so a multitude of poor
may by his strong ones fall.

11He thus hath said within his heart,
The Lord hath quite forgot;
He hides his countenance, and he
for ever sees it not.

12O Lord, do thou arise; O God,
lift up thine hand on high:
Put not the meek afflicted ones
out of thy memory.

13Why is it that the wicked man
thus doth the Lord despise?
Because that God will it require
he in his heart denies.

14Thou hast it seen; for their mischief
and spite thou wilt repay:
The poor commits himself to thee;
thou art the orphan''s stay.

15The arm break of the wicked man,
and of the evil one;
Do thou seek out his wickedness,
until thou findest none.

16The Lord is King through ages all,
ev''n to eternity;
The heathen people from his land
are perish''d utterly.

17O Lord, of those that humble are
thou the desire didst hear;
Thou wilt prepare their heart, and thou
to hear wilt bend thine ear;

18To judge the fatherless, and those
that are oppressed sore;
That man, that is but sprung of earth,
may them oppress no more.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Wherefore is it that thou, O Lord,", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "dost stand from us afar?"}, {"text": "And wherefore hidest thou thyself,", "syllables": ["And", "where-", "-", "fore", "hidest", "thou", "thyse-", "lf,"]}, {"text": "when times so troublous are?"}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked in his loftiness", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "doth persecute the poor:"}, {"text": "In these devices they have fram''d", "syllables": ["In", "these", "de-", "vices", "they", "have", "fra-", "m''d"]}, {"text": "let them be taken sure.", "syllables": ["let", "them", "be", "take-", "n", "sure."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked of his heart''s desire", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "doth talk with boasting great;", "syllables": ["doth", "talk", "with", "boa-", "sting", "great;"]}, {"text": "He blesseth him that''s covetous,", "syllables": ["He", "bles-", "seth", "him", "tha-", "t''s", "cove-", "tous,"]}, {"text": "whom yet the Lord doth hate."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "The wicked, through his pride of face,", "syllables": ["The", "wicked,", "through", "his", "pri-", "de", "of", "face,"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "on God he doth not call;"}, {"text": "And in the counsels of his heart"}, {"text": "the Lord is not at all."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "His ways they always grievous are;", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "thy judgments from his sight"}, {"text": "Removed are: at all his foes"}, {"text": "he puffeth with despight."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Within his heart he thus hath said,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "I shall not moved be;"}, {"text": "And no adversity at all"}, {"text": "shall ever come to me.", "syllables": ["sha-", "ll", "ever", "come", "to", "me."]}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "His mouth with cursing, fraud, deceit,", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "is fill''d abundantly;"}, {"text": "And underneath his tongue there is", "syllables": ["And", "under-", "neath", "his", "ton-", "gue", "there", "is"]}, {"text": "mischief and vanity."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "He closely sits in villages;", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "he slays the innocent:"}, {"text": "Against the poor that pass him by"}, {"text": "his cruel eyes are bent.", "syllables": ["his", "crue-", "l", "eyes", "are", "bent."]}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "He, lion-like, lurks in his den;", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "he waits the poor to take;"}, {"text": "And when he draws him in his net,"}, {"text": "his prey he doth him make."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "Himself he humbleth very low,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "he croucheth down withal,"}, {"text": "That so a multitude of poor"}, {"text": "may by his strong ones fall."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "He thus hath said within his heart,", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "The Lord hath quite forgot;", "syllables": ["The", "Lord", "hath", "quite", "for-", "got;"]}, {"text": "He hides his countenance, and he", "syllables": ["He", "hides", "his", "counte-", "nan-", "ce,", "and", "he"]}, {"text": "for ever sees it not.", "syllables": ["for", "eve-", "r", "sees", "it", "not."]}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord, do thou arise; O God,", "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "lift up thine hand on high:"}, {"text": "Put not the meek afflicted ones"}, {"text": "out of thy memory."}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "Why is it that the wicked man", "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "thus doth the Lord despise?"}, {"text": "Because that God will it require", "syllables": ["because", "that", "God", "will", "it", "requ-", "i-", "re"]}, {"text": "he in his heart denies."}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "Thou hast it seen; for their mischief", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "and spite thou wilt repay:", "syllables": ["and", "spite", "thou", "wilt", "re-", "pay:"]}, {"text": "The poor commits himself to thee;"}, {"text": "thou art the orphan''s stay."}]}, {"index": 14, "lines": [{"text": "The arm break of the wicked man,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "and of the evil one;"}, {"text": "Do thou seek out his wickedness,"}, {"text": "until thou findest none.", "syllables": ["until", "thou", "fin-", "dest", "no-", "ne."]}]}, {"index": 15, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord is King through ages all,", "syllables": ["The", "Lord", "is", "King", "throu-", "gh", "ages", "all,"], "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "ev''n to eternity;", "syllables": ["ev''n", "to", "ete-", "r-", "ni-", "ty;"]}, {"text": "The heathen people from his land", "syllables": ["The", "heathen", "pe-", "o-", "ple", "from", "his", "land"]}, {"text": "are perish''d utterly."}]}, {"index": 16, "lines": [{"text": "O Lord, of those that humble are", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "thou the desire didst hear;"}, {"text": "Thou wilt prepare their heart, and thou"}, {"text": "to hear wilt bend thine ear;"}]}, {"index": 17, "lines": [{"text": "To judge the fatherless, and those", "syllables": ["To", "judge", "the", "fa-", "ther-", "less,", "and", "those"], "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "that are oppressed sore;"}, {"text": "That man, that is but sprung of earth,"}, {"text": "may them oppress no more."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Wherefore is it that thou, O Lord...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (126, 'rechttFUyVpFNogcR', 147, '147', '1Praise ye the Lord; for it is good
praise to our God to sing:
For it is pleasant, and to praise
it is a comely thing.

2God doth build up Jerusalem;
and he it is alone
That the dispers''d of Israel
doth gather into one.

3Those that are broken in their heart,
and grieved in their minds,
He healeth, and their painful wounds
he tenderly up-binds.

4He counts the number of the stars;
he names them ev''ry one.
5Great is our Lord, and of great pow''r;
his wisdom search can none.

6The Lord lifts up the meek; and casts
the wicked to the ground.
7Sing to the Lord, and give him thanks;
on harp his praises sound;

8Who covereth the heav''n with clouds,
who for the earth below
Prepareth rain, who maketh grass
upon the mountains grow.

9He gives the beast his food, he feeds
the ravens young that cry.
10His pleasure not in horses'' strength,
nor in man''s legs, doth lie.

11But in all those that do him fear
the Lord doth pleasure take;
In those that to his mercy do
by hope themselves betake.

12The Lord praise, O Jerusalem;
Sion, thy God confess:
13For thy gates'' bars he maketh strong;
thy sons in thee doth bless.

14He in thy borders maketh peace;
with fine wheat filleth thee.
15He sends forth his command on earth,
his word runs speedily.

16Hoar-frost, like ashes, scatt''reth he;
like wool he snow doth give:
17Like morsels casteth forth his ice;
who in its cold can live?

18He sendeth forth his mighty word,
and melteth them again;
His wind he makes to blow,
and then the waters flow amain.

19The doctrine of his holy word
to Jacob he doth show;
His statutes and his judgments he
gives Israel to know.

20To any nation never he
such favour did afford;
For they his judgments have not known.
O do ye praise the Lord.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Praise ye the Lord; for it is good", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "praise to our God to sing:"}, {"text": "For it is pleasant, and to praise"}, {"text": "it is a comely thing."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "God doth build up Jerusalem;", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "and he it is alone"}, {"text": "That the dispers''d of Israel", "syllables": ["That", "the", "dis-", "pe-", "rs''d", "of", "is-", "rael"]}, {"text": "doth gather into one."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Those that are broken in their heart,", "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "and grieved in their minds,"}, {"text": "He healeth, and their painful wounds"}, {"text": "he tenderly up-binds."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "He counts the number of the stars;", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "he names them ev''ry one."}, {"text": "Great is our Lord, and of great pow''r;", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "his wisdom search can none.", "syllables": ["his", "wisdom", "search", "can", "no-", "ne."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord lifts up the meek; and casts", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "the wicked to the ground."}, {"text": "Sing to the Lord, and give him thanks;", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "on harp his praises sound;", "syllables": ["on", "harp", "his", "praise-", "s", "sound;"]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "Who covereth the heav''n with clouds,", "syllables": ["Who", "cove-", "reth", "the", "heav''n", "with", "clou-", "ds,"], "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "who for the earth below"}, {"text": "Prepareth rain, who maketh grass"}, {"text": "upon the mountains grow."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "He gives the beast his food, he feeds", "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "the ravens young that cry.", "syllables": ["the", "rave-", "ns", "young", "that", "cry."]}, {"text": "His pleasure not in horses'' strength,", "bibleVerseRef": 10}, {"text": "nor in man''s legs, doth lie."}]}, {"index": 7, "lines": [{"text": "But in all those that do him fear", "bibleVerseRef": 11}, {"text": "the Lord doth pleasure take;"}, {"text": "In those that to his mercy do"}, {"text": "by hope themselves betake.", "syllables": ["by", "hope", "themsel-", "ves", "be-", "take."]}]}, {"index": 8, "lines": [{"text": "The Lord praise, O Jerusalem;", "syllables": ["The", "Lord", "praise-", ",", "O", "je-", "ru-", "salem;"], "bibleVerseRef": 12}, {"text": "Sion, thy God confess:", "syllables": ["Sio-", "n,", "thy", "God", "con-", "fess:"]}, {"text": "For thy gates'' bars he maketh strong;", "syllables": ["For", "thy", "gates''", "bars", "he", "make-", "eth", "strong;"], "bibleVerseRef": 13}, {"text": "thy sons in thee doth bless."}]}, {"index": 9, "lines": [{"text": "He in thy borders maketh peace;", "bibleVerseRef": 14}, {"text": "with fine wheat filleth thee."}, {"text": "He sends forth his command on earth,", "bibleVerseRef": 15}, {"text": "his word runs speedily."}]}, {"index": 10, "lines": [{"text": "Hoar-frost, like ashes, scatt''reth he;", "syllables": ["hoa-", "r-frost,", "like", "a-", "shes,", "scat-", "t''reth", "he;"], "bibleVerseRef": 16}, {"text": "like wool he snow doth give:"}, {"text": "Like morsels casteth forth his ice;", "bibleVerseRef": 17}, {"text": "who in its cold can live?"}]}, {"index": 11, "lines": [{"text": "He sendeth forth his mighty word,", "bibleVerseRef": 18}, {"text": "and melteth them again;"}, {"text": "His wind he makes to blow,", "syllables": ["His", "wind", "he", "make-", "-", "s", "to", "blow,"]}, {"text": "and then the waters flow amain.", "syllables": ["and", "then", "the", "waters", "flow", "amain."]}]}, {"index": 12, "lines": [{"text": "The doctrine of his holy word", "syllables": ["The", "doctri-", "ne", "of", "his", "ho-", "ly", "word"], "bibleVerseRef": 19}, {"text": "to Jacob he doth show;"}, {"text": "His statutes and his judgments he", "syllables": ["His", "statu-", "tes", "and", "his", "jud-", "gments", "he"]}, {"text": "gives Israel to know.", "syllables": ["give-", "s", "is-", "rael", "to", "know."]}]}, {"index": 13, "lines": [{"text": "To any nation never he", "bibleVerseRef": 20}, {"text": "such favour did afford;"}, {"text": "For they his judgments have not known."}, {"text": "O do ye praise the Lord."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'Praise ye the Lord; for it is good...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (124, 'rechf1C7fXyFBima3', 47, '47', '1All people, clap your hands; to God
with voice of triumph shout:
2For dreadful is the Lord most high,
great King the earth throughout.

3The heathen people under us
he surely shall subdue;
And he shall make the nations
under our feet to bow.

4The lot of our inheritance
chuse out for us shall he,
Of Jacob, whom he loved well,
ev''n the excellency.

5God is with shouts gone up, the Lord
with trumpets sounding high.
6Sing praise to God, sing praise, sing praise,
praise to our King sing ye.

7For God is King of all the earth;
with knowledge praise express.
8God rules the nations: God sits on
his throne of holiness.

9The princes of the people are
assembled willingly;
Ev''n of the God of Abraham
they who the people be.

For why? the shields that do defend
the earth are only his:
They to the Lord belong; yea, he
exalted greatly is.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "All people, clap your hands; to God", "syllables": ["All", "peo-", "ple,", "clap", "your", "hands;", "to", "God"], "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "with voice of triumph shout:", "syllables": ["with", "voice", "of", "triu-", "mph", "shout:"]}, {"text": "For dreadful is the Lord most high,", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "great King the earth throughout."}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "The heathen people under us", "syllables": ["The", "heathen", "pe-", "o-", "ple", "un-", "der", "us"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "he surely shall subdue;"}, {"text": "And he shall make the nations", "syllables": ["And", "he", "sha-", "ll", "make", "the", "na-", "tions"]}, {"text": "under our feet to bow."}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "The lot of our inheritance", "syllables": ["The", "lot", "of", "our", "inhe-", "ri-", "tan-", "ce"], "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "chuse out for us shall he,"}, {"text": "Of Jacob, whom he loved well,"}, {"text": "ev''n the excellency."}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "God is with shouts gone up, the Lord", "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "with trumpets sounding high."}, {"text": "Sing praise to God, sing praise, sing praise,", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "praise to our King sing ye."}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "For God is King of all the earth;", "bibleVerseRef": 7}, {"text": "with knowledge praise express.", "syllables": ["with", "knowled-", "ge", "praise", "ex-", "press."]}, {"text": "God rules the nations: God sits on", "bibleVerseRef": 8}, {"text": "his throne of holiness.", "syllables": ["his", "throne", "of", "ho-", "li-", "ness."]}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "The princes of the people are", "syllables": ["The", "princes", "of", "the", "pe-", "o-", "ple", "are"], "bibleVerseRef": 9}, {"text": "assembled willingly;"}, {"text": "Ev''n of the God of Abraham"}, {"text": "they who the people be.", "syllables": ["they", "who", "the", "peo-", "ple", "be."]}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "For why? the shields that do defend"}, {"text": "the earth are only his:"}, {"text": "They to the Lord belong; yea, he"}, {"text": "exalted greatly is."}]}]', 'CM', NULL, 'All people, clap your hands; to God...');
INSERT INTO public.psalm_versions (id, airtable_id, psalm_id, psalter_number, lyrics_imported_raw, lyrics_structured, meter, version_label, first_line) VALUES (146, 'recmsy43hy5S7JCnZ', 140, '140', '1Lord, from the ill and froward man
give me deliverance,
And do thou safe preserve me from
the man of violence:

2Who in their heart mischievous things
are meditating ever;
And they for war assembled are
continually together.

3Much like unto a serpent''s tongue
their tongues they sharp do make;
And underneath their lips there lies
the poison of a snake.

4Lord, keep me from the wicked''s hands,
from vi''lent men me save;
Who utterly to overthrow
my goings purpos''d have.

5The proud for me a snare have hid,
and cords; yea, they a net
Have by the way-side for me spread;
they gins for me have set.

6I said unto the Lord, Thou art
my God: unto the cry
Of all my supplications,
Lord, do thine ear apply.

7O God the Lord, who art the strength
of my salvation:
A cov''ring in the day of war
my head thou hast put on.

8Unto the wicked man, O Lord,
his wishes do not grant;
Nor further thou his ill device,
lest they themselves should vaunt.

9As for the head and chief of those
about that compass me,
Ev''n by the mischief of their lips
let thou them cover''d be.

10Let burning coals upon them fall,
them throw in fiery flame,
And in deep pits, that they no more
may rise out of the same.

11Let not an evil speaker be
on earth established:
Mischief shall hunt the vi''lent man,
till he be ruined.

12I know God will th'' afflicted''s cause
maintain, and poor men''s right.
13Surely the just shall praise thy name;
th'' upright dwell in thy sight.', '[{"index": 0, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, from the ill and froward man", "bibleVerseRef": 1}, {"text": "give me deliverance,", "syllables": ["give", "me", "deli-", "ve-", "ran-", "ce,"]}, {"text": "And do thou safe preserve me from"}, {"text": "the man of violence:", "syllables": ["the", "man", "of", "viole-", "n-", "ce:"]}]}, {"index": 1, "lines": [{"text": "Who in their heart mischievous things", "bibleVerseRef": 2}, {"text": "are meditating ever;"}, {"text": "And they for war assembled are"}, {"text": "continually together.", "syllables": ["continu-", "a-", "lly", "to-", "ge-", "ther."]}]}, {"index": 2, "lines": [{"text": "Much like unto a serpent''s tongue", "syllables": ["Much", "like", "unto", "a", "ser-", "pent''s", "ton-", "gue"], "bibleVerseRef": 3}, {"text": "their tongues they sharp do make;"}, {"text": "And underneath their lips there lies"}, {"text": "the poison of a snake.", "syllables": ["the", "poison", "of", "a", "sna-", "ke."]}]}, {"index": 3, "lines": [{"text": "Lord, keep me from the wicked''s hands,", "bibleVerseRef": 4}, {"text": "from vi''lent men me save;"}, {"text": "Who utterly to overthrow", "syllables": ["Who", "ut-", "ter-", "ly", "to", "ove-", "r-", "throw"]}, {"text": "my goings purpos''d have.", "syllables": ["my", "goi-", "ngs", "pur-", "pos''d", "have."]}]}, {"index": 4, "lines": [{"text": "The proud for me a snare have hid,", "syllables": ["The", "proud", "for", "me", "a", "snare", "have", "hid,"], "bibleVerseRef": 5}, {"text": "and cords; yea, they a net"}, {"text": "Have by the way-side for me spread;"}, {"text": "they gins for me have set."}]}, {"index": 5, "lines": [{"text": "I said unto the Lord, Thou art", "bibleVerseRef": 6}, {"text": "my God: unto the cry"}, {"text": "Of all my supplications,", "syllables": ["Of", "all", "my", "sup-", "pli-", "ca-", "tio-", "ns,"]}, {"text": "Lord, do thine ear apply."}]}, {"index": 6, "lines": [{"text": "O God the Lord, who art the strength", "bibleVerseRe